hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5401","He said: And we used to greet in prayer, and it was said to us: Indeed in prayer there is occupation."
"5402","Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from Sayyar Abu al-Hakam, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is afflicted by poverty and presents it to people, his poverty will not be remedied; and whoever presents it to Allah, He will soon grant him sufficiency, either soon or later."
"5403","And from Muhammad ibn Bishr and al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl, they said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys, we heard a caller calling: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the fitra. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. The Prophet said: He has come out of the Fire. So we hastened to him, and he was a herdsman whom prayer overtook, so he called for it."
"5404","Abu Musa al-Harawi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Umar ibn Amir narrated to me, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Yahya al-Jabir, from Abu Majida al-Ijli, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People pardon one another for prescribed punishments as long as they are not raised to the rulers; when raised to the ruler, he judges between them by the Book of Allah."
"5405","Abu Musa narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zir, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will emerge a people in the end of time, young in age, foolish in minds, speaking the best of speech, reciting the Quran not passing their throats, passing through Islam as the arrow passes through the target. Whoever meets them should fight them, for killing them is a reward with Allah for whoever kills them."
"5406","Sahl ibn Zanjala ar-Razi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his brother, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters; for every letter thereof is an outer and an inner."
"5407","Abdul Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Yahya al-Jabir, from Abu Majida, from Abdullah, he said: We asked our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about walking with the funeral, and he said: Less than trotting; if it be good, it is hastened to it, and if it be other than that, then away with the people of the Fire. The funeral is followed and does not follow; whoever precedes it is not of it."
"5408","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from al-Qasim ibn Abdur Rahman: that Ibn Mas'ud sold some slaves of the governorship to al-Ash'ath, then came to demand payment from him, and they differed over the price. Ibn Mas'ud said: Will you accept that I judge between me and you by the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? When the two sellers differ, the word is what the seller says, or they annul."
"5409","Abu Yasir Ammar ibn Nasr narrated to us, Ali ibn Abis an-Nakha'i Abu al-Hasan narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early mornings."
"5410","Abdur Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubayda, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that he said: When there was revealed: When the help of Allah comes and the victory, to the end of the sura, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say frequently: Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me; indeed You are the Oft-Returning."
"5411","Abdur Rahman ibn Sallam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayra ibn Yarim, from Abdullah: that he said: Whoever comes to a diviner, a magician, or a soothsayer, asks him and believes him in what he says, has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5412","Ja'far ibn Mihran as-Sabbak narrated to us, Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from his father, from Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My nation has been blessed in its early mornings."
"5413","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurara narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit, we faced him with our faces."
"5414","Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Zurara, Kufan, narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'ida narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Fudayl, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdullah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept until he snored, then stood and prayed. He said: I mentioned it to Ata, and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not like others."
"5415","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not refuse gifts, answer the inviter, and do not beat Muslims."
"5416","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abdur Rahman narrated to us, Isa narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Qays al-Awdi, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine two prayers while traveling."
"5417","Qasim ibn Abi Ubayd narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first for which the servant will be reckoned is prayer, and the first judged among people on the Day of Resurrection is blood."
"5418","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, az-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until their ripeness appears, and forbade selling fruits for dates."
"5419","Ibn Umar said: Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted ariya transactions."
"5420","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, az-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah gave the Quran, and he stands with it night and day; and a man to whom Allah gave wealth, and he spends it night and day."
"5421","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"5422","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from az-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: A man saw that Laylat al-Qadr is the night of the twenty-seventh, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see your dreams agree upon the last ten, so seek it in the odd nights thereof."
"5423","And from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he opened prayer raise his hands level with his shoulders, and when he bowed, and when he raised, and he does not raise between the two prostrations."
"5424","And from his father: that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar walking in front of the funeral."
"5425","And from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when travel hastened him, he combined Maghrib and Isha."
"5426","And from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed as miqat Dhu al-Hulayfah for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Sham, Qarn for the people of Najd, and it was mentioned to Ibn Umar though he had not heard it, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen."
"5427","And from his father: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man admonishing his brother about modesty, so he said: Modesty is part of faith."
"5428","And from al-Zuhri, he heard Salim narrating from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what clothing the muhrim wears. He said: He does not wear the shirt, nor the turban, nor the hooded cloak, nor trousers, nor any garment touched by saffron or wars, nor leather socks except for one who cannot find sandals; whoever cannot find sandals, let him cut them below the ankles."
"5429","And from al-Zuhri, he heard Salim narrating from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not prevent her. Sufyan said: They considered that to be at night."
"5430","And from al-Zuhri, Salim informed me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it; and whoever sells palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it."
"5431","And from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five incur no sin on whoever kills them in the Sanctuary and in ihram: the mouse, the crow, the kite, the scorpion, and the vicious dog."
"5432","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: We heard al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Kill snakes, and the one with two stripes and the tailless one, for they efface eyesight and cause miscarriage. He said: And Abdullah used to kill every snake he found."
"5433","And from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: By Allah, I never swore by them afterward, neither quoting nor initiating."
"5434","And from Salim, from his father: he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The night prayer is two by two, so if you fear dawn, pray witr with one."
"5435","And from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."
"5436","And from Salim, from his father: it was said to him, Do you raise it to the Prophet? He said: Yes. He said: Ill omen is in three: in the horse, the woman, and the house."
"5437","And from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"5438","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs after Friday prayer."
"5439","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will find people like a hundred camels among which there is hardly a mount fit for riding."
"5440","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi accepted Islam while married to ten women, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Choose four of them. Then in the time of Umar he divorced his wives and divided his wealth among his sons; that reached Umar, so he met him and said: I suspect Satan has heard of your death through eavesdropping and cast it into your soul, and perhaps you will live only a little. By Allah, you will take back your wives and take back your wealth, or I will bequeath it to them, and I will order your grave to be stoned as the grave of Abu Righal was stoned."
"5441","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Salim, from his father, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rakahs."
"5442","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the two prayers at Muzdalifah, praying each with an iqamah, and he did not offer any voluntary prayer before either of them or after."
"5443","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar: that he divorced his wife while menstruating, so Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Order him to take her back, then let him divorce her while she is pure or pregnant."
"5444","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his deeds every day. He said: And Salim said: Abu Hurayrah said: Or a farm dog. He said: And he owned farmland."
"5445","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"5446","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If your women ask your permission to go to the mosques, give them permission."
"5447","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me, a house will be built for him in the Fire."
"5448","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to lighten the prayer, yet he would lead us in Fajr prayer with al-Saffat."
"5449","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Musa, he said: I was with Salim ibn Abdullah on a journey when a caravan of Umm al-Banin passed with bells, so Salim narrated from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels do not accompany a party in which there is a jingling bell; so how many jingles are in this one?!"
"5450","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"5451","Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break your fast; if it is obscured from you, estimate for it. He said: Salim said: Abdullah used to fast a day before the crescent when it was obscured."
"5452","Abu Amir Hawtharah ibn Ashras narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Abi al-Sahba Abu Khuraym al-Bahili narrated to us, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr then faced the sunrise and said: Indeed tribulations come from here, three times, and from there rises the horn of Satan."
"5453","Abu Amir narrated to us, Uqbah, meaning Ibn Abi al-Sahba, informed me, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among a group of his Companions, and the Messenger of Allah turned to them and said: Do you not know that I am the Messenger of Allah to you? They said: Yes, we bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not know that whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and obedience to me is part of obedience to Allah? They said: Yes, we bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed Allah, and obedience to you is part of obedience to Allah. He said: Then part of obedience to Allah is to obey me, and part of obedience to me is to obey your commanders; obey your commanders, and if they pray sitting, then pray sitting."
"5454","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: A man from Sham sat with Abdullah ibn Umar while I was with him, and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what do you think about tamattu, combining Umrah with Hajj? Abdullah said to him: It is good and fine for whoever does it. The man said: But your father used to forbid it. So Abdullah became angry, then said: Woe to you, if my father forbade it while the Messenger of Allah practiced it, do you follow the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or the command of my father? He said: No, rather the command of the Messenger of Allah. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it, so go about your business."
"5455","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break your fast; if it is obscured from you, estimate. And Abdullah used to fast a day before the crescent."
"5456","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"5457","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Your remaining lifespan compared to the nations before you is like the time between Asr prayer and sunset: the people of the Torah were given the Torah and worked until midday then failed, and were given a qirat each; then the people of the Gospel were given the Gospel and worked until Asr prayer, then failed and were given a qirat each; then we were given the Quran and worked until sunset, and were given two qirats each; so the people of the two Books said: O our Lord, why did You give them two qirats each and give us one qirat each, while we worked more than them? Allah said: Have I wronged you anything of your wages? They said: No. He said: It is My bounty, I give it to whom I will."
"5458","And from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Abdullah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not trade dates on the tree for picked dates, and do not trade fruit until its soundness appears. He said: And neither the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar appointed a judge, until the end of his time, when he said to Yazid ibn Ukht Namir: Spare me some matters, meaning the minor ones."
"5459","And from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The keys of the unseen are five: Indeed with Allah is knowledge of the Hour, He sends down rain, knows what is in the wombs, no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die; indeed Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."
"5460","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People are like a hundred camels among which you can hardly find a mount fit for riding."
"5461","And from Salim, he heard Abdullah ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah never said red about Jesus, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was asleep I saw myself circumambulating the Kabah, when there was a wheat-complexioned man with straight hair, between two men, water dripping from his head, or his head pouring forth; I said: Who is this? They said: This is the son of Mary. I turned, and there was a red, bulky man with curly hair, blind in the right eye, as if his eye were a floating grape. I said: Who is this? They said: The Dajjal; the person most resembling him is a man from Khuzah called Ibn Qatan. Muhammad said: He is from Banu al-Mustaliq, and died in Jahiliyyah."
"5462","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr on his mount."
"5463","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was approached while at al-Muarras in Dhu al-Hulayfah in the valley, and it was said to him: You are in a blessed valley floor."
"5464","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi and Salim: that Ibn Umar, whenever he passed Dhu al-Hulayfah, would spend the night there until morning, and would report that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"5465","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Salim narrated to me, from his father, that he used to narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he appointed Usamah ibn Zayd; news reached him that people criticized Usamah and impugned his command, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, as Salim narrated to me, and said: You criticize Usamah and impugn his command, yet you did the same with his father before; he was well fit for command, and he is the most beloved of all people to me, and this son of his is the most beloved of people to me; treat him well, for he is among the best of you. Salim said: I never heard Abdullah narrate this hadith without saying: Except Fatimah."
"5466","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Asim ibn Ubaydullah said: he informed me, he said: I heard Salim narrating from Ibn Umar: that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, what about what we do, is it in a matter already decreed or in a new, unprecedented matter? He said: In what has already been decreed, Shubah doubted, so act, O son of Khattab, for everyone is facilitated: whoever is among the people of felicity will act for felicity, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will act for wretchedness."
"5467","Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from the nephew of Ibn Shihab, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman used to walk in front of the funeral bier."
"5468","Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi and Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of domestic donkeys."
"5469","Muhammad ibn Bakkar Abu Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"5470","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi al-Madani narrated to us, from Asim, from Bilal ibn Abi Bakr, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden, its little and its much are alike."
"5471","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Anas, meaning Ibn Iyad, narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, that Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever sells a slave, his property belongs to the one who sold him unless the buyer stipulates it; and whoever sells pollinated palm trees, their fruit belongs to the one who sold them unless the buyer stipulates it."
"5472","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Fulayh, narrated to me, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah said, and Ibn Shihab said: Salim ibn Abdullah informed me, that Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: While I was asleep I saw myself circumambulating the Kabah, when there was a man with straight hair between two men, his head dripping, or pouring forth, water. I said: Who is this? They said: The son of Mary. I turned, and there was a red, bulky man with curly hair, blind, as if his eye were a floating grape. I said: Who is this? They said: The Dajjal; the person most resembling him is Ibn Qatan."
"5473","Mujahid ibn Musa al-Khuttalli narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote the book of charity and kept it with his sword; he did not send it out to his agents until he died, then Abu Bakr acted by it until he died, then Umar acted by it. In it was: for five camels, one sheep; for ten, two sheep; for fifteen, three sheep; for twenty, four sheep; for twenty-five, a one-year-old she-camel up to thirty-five; if more, a two-year-old she-camel up to forty-five; if more, a three-year-old she-camel up to sixty; if more, a four-year-old she-camel up to seventy-five; if more, two two-year-old she-camels up to ninety; if more, two three-year-old she-camels up to one hundred twenty; if more than one hundred twenty, for every fifty, a three-year-old she-camel, and for every forty, a two-year-old she-camel. And for sheep charity: for every forty sheep, one sheep up to one hundred twenty; if more, two sheep up to two hundred; if more, three sheep up to three hundred; if more, for every hundred sheep, one sheep; nothing is due until it reaches one hundred; what is together must not be separated, nor what is separate joined, out of fear of charity; and whatever belongs to two partners, they settle evenly between them; and no decrepit or defective animal is taken in charity. Sufyan said: Al-Zuhri did not mention cattle. Al-Zuhri said: When the collector comes, he divides the wealth into thirds: a third of the best, a third of the worst, and a third of the middle, taking from the middle."
"5474","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, with its chain, similar to it."
"5475","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Musa, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The oath of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he swore by was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"5476","Zuhayr narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch except the two Yemeni corners."
"5477","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi and Salim: that Ibn Umar, whenever he passed Dhu al-Hulayfah, would spend the night there until morning, and would report that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"5478","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, the people of Najd from Qarn. He said: And it was mentioned to me, though I did not hear it, he said: And the people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam."
"5479","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit for dates."
"5480","He said: So Zayd ibn Thabit informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted arayas."
"5481","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah has given wealth, and he spends from it night and day; and a man to whom Allah has given the Quran, and he stands with it night and day."
"5482","And from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever buys palm trees after they have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it; and whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it."
"5483","And from Salim, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said on the pulpit: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"5484","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands to the shoulders when he began prayer, when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing; and he did not raise them between the two prostrations."
"5485","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar walking in front of the funeral bier."
"5486","And from Salim, from his father: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Umar swearing by his father, so he said: Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. So Umar said: By Allah, I never swore by them afterward, neither initiating nor quoting."
"5487","And from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see your dreams have coincided about the last ten nights, so seek it in the remaining seven or in the odd nights among them."
"5488","And from Salim, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combining Maghrib and Isha when travel pressed him."
"5489","And from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"5490","And from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he heard a man admonishing his brother about modesty, so he said to him: Modesty is part of faith."
"5491","And from Salim, from his father: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what clothing the muhrim wears. He said: Do not wear shirts, nor trousers, nor turbans, nor hooded cloaks, nor any garment touched by wars or saffron, and do not wear leather socks except a man who has no sandals, then let him cut them below the ankles."
"5492","And from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its soundness appears."
"5493","And from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Ill omen is in three: in the house, the mount, and the woman."
"5494","And from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: If the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not prevent her. Amr said: Sufyan said: A man said: From Nafi, he explained it as at night."
"5495","Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until you hear the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum."
"5496","Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill snakes, and the one with two stripes and the tailless one, for they seek eyesight and cause miscarriage; and Ibn Umar used to kill every snake he found, then Abu Lubabah ibn Abd al-Mundhir, or Zayd ibn al-Khattab, saw him chasing a snake and said: It has been forbidden to kill house snakes."
"5497","Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The night prayer is two by two, so if you fear dawn, pray witr with one rakah which makes odd what has passed."
"5498","And from Salim, from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"5499","Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The one who misses the prayer, the Asr prayer, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"5500","Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what animals the muhrim may kill. He said: Five animals incur no sin on whoever kills them in the Sanctuary and outside it: the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, the kite, and the vicious dog."
"5501","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Kill snakes, and kill the one with two stripes and the tailless one, for they take away eyesight and abort fetuses. Abdullah ibn Umar said: While I was chasing a snake, Abu Lubabah saw me, and Abu Lubabah said... I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered killing them, so Abu Lubabah said: He forbade it afterward."
"5502","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father Abdullah ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from bowing, would raise his hands and say: Allah hears whoever praises Him; our Lord, to You belongs praise."
"5503","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi: that Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah and Salim ibn Abdullah informed him that they spoke to Abdullah on the nights the army descended upon Ibn al-Zubayr before he was killed, saying: It will not harm you to skip Hajj this year; we fear you will be blocked from the House. He said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the disbelievers of Quraysh blocked us from the House, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed his offering and shaved his head; and I call you to witness that I have obligated an Umrah; if Allah wills I shall proceed: if I am left free between me and the House I shall circumambulate, and if I am blocked from it I shall do as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did while I was with him. So he entered ihram for Umrah at Dhu al-Hulayfah, then traveled a while and said: The two are the same matter; and I call you to witness that I have obligated a Hajj with my Umrah. He did not release from either until he released on the Day of Sacrifice; and he used to say: Whoever combines Hajj and Umrah and enters ihram for both, he does not release until he releases from both together on the Day of Sacrifice, circumambulating for both one tawaf of the House, and of Safa and Marwah on the day he enters Makkah."
"5504","Abdullah ibn Abd al-Samad, or Salih ibn Abd al-Samad his brother, narrated to us, Qasim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking permission for Umrah, so he said: O my brother, supplicate, and do not forget us in righteous supplication."
"5505","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Asram ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the shadow is a cubit and a half to two cubits, pray Zuhr."
"5506","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted the Muslims about what would gather them for prayer; they said: The horn. He disliked it because of the Jews. Then the bell was mentioned, and he disliked it because of the Christians. That night a man from the Ansar called Abdullah ibn Zayd, and Umar ibn al-Khattab, was shown the call to prayer; the Ansari knocked on his door, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, who called the adhan with it. Al-Zuhri said: And Bilal added to the dawn call: Prayer is better than sleep, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approved it; and Umar said: I had seen the like of what he saw, but he preceded me."
"5507","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses Asr, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"5508","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses Asr, it is as if he has been deprived of his family and his wealth."
"5509","Nuaym ibn Haydam narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, Abu Matar narrated to me, that he heard Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrating from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard thunder and thunderbolts, he said: O Allah, do not kill us with Your anger, nor destroy us with Your punishment, and grant us health before that."
"5510","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever sells a slave who has property, his property belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it; and whoever sells pollinated palm trees, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates it."
"5511","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Talhah, meaning Ibn Yahya, narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not raise your eyes to the sky lest they be snatched."
"5512","Abdullah ibn Umar al-Kufi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hanzalah, he said: I heard Salim saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If your women ask your permission to go to the mosques, give them permission."
"5513","Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala al-Kufi narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Tribulation comes from here, and he gestured with his hand toward the east, where the horn of Satan rises; and you will strike one another's necks. And Musa only killed the one he killed from Pharaoh's people by mistake; Allah said to him: And you killed a soul, then We saved you from distress and tried you thoroughly."
"5514","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from Burd ibn Sinan, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one should spend three nights without having his will with him. He said: So I never spent a night without my will placed with me, or as he said."
"5515","Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan informed me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Hajj or Umrah, whenever he came upon a highland or a pass, he would say takbir three times, then say: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; to Him belongs dominion and praise; He gives life and death, and He is over all things Capable; returning, repenting, praising our Lord; Allah has fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the confederates alone."
"5516","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from Salim, from Abdullah ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was shown in sleep that I was drawing water with a bucket at a well; then Abu Bakr came and drew one or two buckets, drawing weakly, and Allah forgives him; then Umar came and drew, and it turned into a large bucket; I never saw a strong genius among people working like his work, until the people drank their fill and watered their camels."
"5517","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, he said: I heard Salim, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Usamah came out wearing a suit, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tear it into headscarves for your family."
"5518","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, Hanzalah narrated to us, he said: I heard Salim, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That the belly of the son of Adam be filled with pus is better for him than being filled with poetry."
"5519","Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys pollinated palm trees without stipulating their fruit, he gets nothing; and whoever buys a slave without stipulating his property, he gets nothing."
"5520","Yaqub ibn al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Sulayman Abu Sulayman, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Usamah ibn Zayd, people spoke about him. He said: That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or something of it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What you said about Usamah has reached me, and you said the same about his father before him; he is well fit for command, he is well fit for command, he is well fit for command, and he is the most beloved of people to me. He said: And he did not except Fatimah nor anyone else."
"5521","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Bakri narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, Ibn Shihab informed me, Salim ibn Abdullah informed me, from Abdullah ibn Umar: that he used to walk in front of the funeral bier, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman used to walk ahead of it."
"5522","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The oath of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: No, by the Disposer of hearts."
"5523","Husayn ibn al-Aswad al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Said narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The oath of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by which he swore was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"5524","Al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Salim informed me, Abdullah ibn Umar informed me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought Hatib ibn Abi Baltaah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you write this letter? He said: Yes; by Allah, it was not, O Messenger of Allah, out of disbelief in my heart, but there was no one among Quraysh except he had family and servants protecting his family for him, so I wrote a letter hoping Allah would thereby protect my family. Umar said: Permit me regarding him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Would you kill him? He said: Yes, if you permit me regarding him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How do you know; perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish."
"5525","Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: I heard Salim saying: Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will fight the Jews until the stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew behind me, come and kill him."
"5526","Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw people gathered for reckoning; Abu Bakr stood and drew one or two buckets, with weakness in his drawing, and Allah forgives him; then Umar stood and it turned into a large bucket; I never saw a strong genius among people working like his work, until the people watered their camels. He said: And al-abqari means the hired hand."
"5527","Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw a black woman with disheveled hair coming out of Madinah until she reached Mahyaah, which is al-Juhfah; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interpreted the dream: the epidemic of Madinah moving to al-Juhfah."
"5528","Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, and Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys."
"5529","Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Jizi narrated to us, Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, a shaykh from Madinah narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his supplication: A protection like the protection of the newborn. Abu Yala said: Meaning the newborn child, and so it was explained to us."
"5530","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Zakariyya, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Selling fruit is not valid until its soundness appears."
"5531","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the pulpit: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"5532","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him, would combine Maghrib and Isha."
"5533","And with it, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"5534","And from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar walking in front of the funeral bier."
"5535","And from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked what clothing the muhrim wears. He said: He does not wear the shirt, nor the turban, nor the hooded cloak, nor trousers, nor any garment touched by saffron or wars, nor leather socks except for one who cannot find sandals; whoever cannot find sandals, let him cut them so they are below the ankles."
"5536","And from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began prayer, raising his hands level with his shoulders, and when he intended to bow, and after bowing; and he did not raise them between the two prostrations."
"5537","And from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ill omen is in three: in the horse, the woman, and the house."
"5538","And from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man admonishing his brother about modesty, so he said: Modesty is part of faith."
"5539","And from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Umar saying: By my father, by my father; so he said: Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. Umar said: By Allah, I never swore by them afterward, neither quoting nor initiating."
"5540","And from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"5541","And from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not prevent her. Sufyan said: They explained it as at night."
"5542","And from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill snakes, and the one with two stripes and the tailless one, for they seek eyesight and abort fetuses; and Ibn Umar used to kill every snake he found, then Abu Lubabah, or Zayd ibn al-Khattab, saw him chasing a snake and said: He forbade house snakes."
"5543","And from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until you hear Ibn Umm Maktum."
"5544","And from his father, he said: A man saw that Laylat al-Qadr was such-and-such night of the ten, meaning Laylat al-Qadr, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: I see your dreams have coincided that it is in the last ten; so seek it in the last ten, in the odd nights among them."
"5545","And from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah has given the Quran, and he stands with it night and day; and a man to whom Allah has given wealth, and he spends it night and day."
"5546","And from his father, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five animals incur no sin on whoever kills them in ihram and the Sanctuary: the crow, the mouse, the scorpion, the vicious dog. Sufyan said: And the lion, the wolf, and the stinging hornet."
"5547","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a white shirt on Umar and said: Is your shirt new or washed? He said: I think he said: Washed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wear new, live praiseworthy, and die a martyr."
"5548","And with it, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No man should let three nights pass without having his will with him. Abd al-Razzaq said: Never did three nights pass me without my will being with me."
"5549","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed so-and-so and so-and-so in Fajr prayer, people among the hypocrites, so Allah revealed: You have nothing to do with the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"5550","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa, from Salim, from his father, he said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"5551","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People are like a hundred camels among which there is no mount fit for riding."
"5552","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permission for Umrah, so he permitted him. He said: O my brother, include us in your righteous supplication and do not forget us."
"5553","Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, that Abu Qilabah narrated to him, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A fire will emerge from the sea of Hadramawt, or from Hadramawt, driving the people. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us? He said: Upon you is Sham."
"5554","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Harmalah, informed me, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog except a livestock dog or a hunting dog, one qirat is deducted from his deeds every day. Abdullah said: And Abu Hurayrah said: Or a farm dog."
"5555","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Shababab ibn Sawwar and Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to lighten the prayer, though he would lead us in Fajr with al-Saffat."
"5556","Al-Fadl ibn al-Sabbah narrated to me, Man ibn Isa narrated to me, Khalid ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gate of my ummah through which it enters Paradise is as wide as a well-ridden rider's three-day journey; they will be pressed upon it until their shoulders almost shift."
"5557","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to glorify Allah while on the back of his mount wherever it faced. Abu Yala said: Meaning he prayed."
"5558","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will not enter Paradise, and three Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: the disobedient to his parents, the cuckold, and the masculinized woman; and three Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, repeating the disobedient to his parents, and the habitual drinker, and the one who reminds others of his gifts."
"5559","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Matar narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, he said: I traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and with Umar, and they never added to two rakahs; and we were astray, so Allah guided us, so by him we follow."
"5560","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Hamzah, he said: I heard Ikrimah saying: Both hands of Allah are right hands; He will fold the heavens and take them in His hand, then say: I am the King; where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant? He said: Then He will take the earths in His other hand and say: I am the King; where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant? Umar said: So I narrated this hadith to Salim ibn Abdullah, and Salim said: Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will fold the heavens on the Day of Resurrection, then take them in His right hand, then say: I am the King; where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant? Then He will fold the earths, then take them in His left, then say: I am the King; where are the tyrants? Where are the arrogant?"
"5561","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Nukri narrated to us, Mubashshir, meaning Ibn Ismail al-Halabi, narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the wife of one of you asks his permission to go to the mosque, let him not prevent her."
"5562","Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn Dawud, narrated to us, from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever keeps a dog except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day. Abu Hurayrah said: Or a farm dog. He said: And Abu Hurayrah used to farm."
"5563","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Dawud informed us, from Hanzalah, from Salim: that Ibn Umar divorced his wife while menstruating, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to take her back."
"5564","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd al-Madani narrated to us, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah narrating from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not foul-mouthed."
"5565","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from al-Zuhri: that Salim ibn Abdullah narrated to him, that he heard a man from Sham asking Abdullah ibn Umar about one performing tamattu with Umrah to Hajj; Abdullah said: It is lawful. The Syrian said: But your father forbade it. Abdullah said: What if my father forbade it while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced it; do you follow the command of my father or the command of the Messenger of Allah? The Syrian said: Rather the command of the Messenger of Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) practiced it."
"5566","Ahmad ibn al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered prayer, raising his hands, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing; and he did not do that in prostration."
"5567","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab: that Salim ibn Abdullah informed him, that Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah at the start, and prayed in its mosque."
"5568","Al-Hasan ibn Ismail narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your remaining lifespan compared to the nations before you is like the time between Asr prayer and sunset: the people of the Torah were given the Torah and worked until midday then failed, and were given a qirat each; the Christians were given the Gospel and worked until Asr prayer then failed, and were given a qirat each; then we were given the Quran and worked from Asr prayer until sunset, and were given two qirats each; so the Jews and Christians said: O our Lord, we worked more than them yet You gave us one qirat each. So He, Blessed and Exalted, said: Have I wronged you anything of your wages? They said: No. He said: It is My bounty, I give it to whom I will."
"5569","Sulayman ibn Umar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Wazi, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats any of this meat, let him wash his hand of its smell and grease, so as not to harm whoever is beside him."
"5570","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Abu Aqil, meaning Yahya ibn al-Mutawakkil, narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Ubaydullah informed us, from Salim, from his father Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not eat with your left hands, nor drink with them, for Satan eats with them and drinks with them."
"5571","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to glorify Allah while on the back of his riding animal, whichever direction it faced. Abu Ya'la said: i.e. he would pray voluntary prayer."
"5572","Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: O people of Iraq, how little you ask about minor matters and how you leave major matters! I heard my father Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Tribulation will come from here, and he gestured with his hand toward the east, and you will strike one another's necks. Musa only killed the one he killed of Pharaoh's household by mistake. Allah said: {And you killed a soul, then We saved you from distress and tried you with trials}."
"5573","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Zimmani narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Asim ibn Ubayd Allah informed me, he said: I heard the son of Abd Allah ibn Umar narrating from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about what we do: is it a matter already decided and finished, or a matter newly begun? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather it is what has already been finished. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then should we not rely on that? He said: Act, for everyone is facilitated. Whoever is of the people of happiness will act for happiness, and whoever is of the people of misery will act for misery."
"5574","Abu al-Fadl Shuja' ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5575","And with the same chain I heard Ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For the belly of one of you to be filled with pus is better for him than for it to be filled with poetry."
"5576","Rawh ibn Abd al-Mu'min narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: (And with Him is knowledge of the Book)."
"5577","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus narrating from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves unless you are weeping, lest there befall you the like of what befell them, meaning the people of al-Hijr."
"5578","Zuhayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no infection without Allah's decree and no bad omens."
"5579","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stoned the first jamrah next to the mosque, the mosque of Mina, would stone it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble, then he would go forward in front of it and stand facing the qiblah raising his hands supplicating, and he would prolong the standing, then he would come to the second jamrah and stone it with seven pebbles saying takbir with each pebble, then he would go down to the left side toward the valley and stand facing the qiblah raising his hands supplicating, then he would come to the jamrah at al-Aqabah and stone it with seven pebbles saying takbir with each pebble, then he would leave and not stand at it. Al-Zuhri said: I heard Salim narrating this from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ibn Umar used to do it."
"5580","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Hanzalah al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When your women ask your permission to go to the mosque, permit them."
"5581","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to grant additional spoils to some of those he sent on expeditions, for themselves exclusively, apart from the share of the general army, and the fifth is obligatory in all of that."
"5582","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant makes an image except that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Give life to what you created."
"5583","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muslim, from Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging will persist with a man until he meets Allah with no flesh on his face."
"5584","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Bunani narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, Hamzah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar informed me that he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When punishment descends upon a people, the punishment strikes whoever is among them, then they will be resurrected according to their deeds."
"5585","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed wine, and cursed its drinker, its pourer, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the eater of its price."
"5586","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubayd Allah, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and when he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left. Zuhayr said: He is Ibn Umar."
"5587","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad al-Umari narrated to us, that his father narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise go to Paradise and the people of Hell go to Hell, death will be brought until it is placed between Paradise and Hell, then it will be slaughtered, then a caller will call: O people of Paradise, no death; O people of Hell, no death. So the people of Paradise will increase in joy upon their joy, and the people of Hell in sorrow upon their sorrow."
"5588","Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed me, that his father narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: We were talking about the Farewell Pilgrimage while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us, and we did not know what the Farewell Pilgrimage was. So the Messenger of Allah praised Allah alone and extolled Him, then he mentioned the Dajjal, the False Messiah, and spoke at length about him, then he said: Allah has not sent a prophet except that he warned his nation of him. Nuh warned of him, and the prophets after him. He will emerge among you, and whatever of his affair is hidden from you, it is not hidden from you that he is blind in his right eye as if it is a floating grape. Then he said: Allah has made your blood and wealth sacred to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness. Then he said: Woe to you - or woe upon you - look, do not return after me as disbelievers striking one another's necks."
"5589","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Bashshar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An oath only leads to expiation or regret."
"5590","Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to pray on his riding animal wherever it turned with him."
"5591","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: I heard my father saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This rule will remain with Quraysh as long as two people remain among mankind."
"5592","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about water in open land frequented by riding animals and beasts, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When water reaches the amount of two qullahs, it does not carry filth."
"5593","Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed wine, its drinker, its pourer, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, and the eater of its price."
"5594","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not return after me as disbelievers striking one another's necks."
"5595","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Asadi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Muhammad, from Waqid, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: How will you be, O Abd Allah ibn Umar, when you remain among the dregs of people whose covenants and trusts have been corrupted, and they differ and become like this? And he interlaced his fingers. He said: What then, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Take what you know, leave what you reject, attend to your own affairs, and leave the common folk."
"5596","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Abd al-Muttalib ibn Abd Allah al-Makhzumi, he said: A man came to Abd Allah ibn Umar and said: How do I pray witr? He said: Pray witr with one rak'ah. He said: I fear people will say it is al-butayra (deficient). He said: Do you want the Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger? This is the Sunnah of Allah and the Sunnah of His Messenger."
"5597","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from his father, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about fasting the Day of Arafah. He said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and Umar and they did not fast it, and I performed Hajj with Uthman and he did not fast it, and I do not fast it, nor do I command it nor forbid it."
"5598","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition, so we fled in panic, then we entered Madinah and hid. He said: We said: We are ruined, O Messenger of Allah, we are the deserters. He said: No, rather you are those who return to fight, and I am your support. Abu Ali said: And Ibn Fudayl added in it, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar, he said: And we kissed his hand, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5599","Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Mudhakkir narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim al-Ammi narrated to us, from his father, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution washing once each, and said: This is the ablution without which Allah does not accept prayer. Then he performed ablution washing twice each, and said: This is the moderate ablution; its doer is given double reward. Then he performed ablution washing three times each, and said: This is my ablution, and the ablution of Ibrahim the Friend of Allah, and the ablution of the prophets before me, and it is the prescribed ablution. Whoever performs my ablution like this, then says: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, eight gates of Paradise will be opened for him, he may enter through whichever he wishes."
"5600","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Kulayb ibn Wa'il, from Habib ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: Did Uthman attend Badr? He said: No. He said: Did he attend the Pledge of Ridwan? He said: No. He said: Was he among those who turned away on the day the two armies met? He said: Yes. He said: So he left, and it was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, this man will report that you disparaged Uthman. He said: Bring him back to me. Ibn Umar said to him: As for the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left him behind for his need and allotted him a share, and he would not allot to one absent. As for the Pledge of Ridwan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him to the people of Makkah, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought out his hands and wiped them over his palm and said: This is for Uthman, for the hand of the Messenger of Allah is better than the hand of Uthman. As for the day the two armies met, Allah has pardoned them. Go and exert your utmost against me."
"5601","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Fudayl, from Atiyyah, from Ibn Umar, he said: One prostration of yours is longer than three prostrations of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5602","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dawud informed us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Umar ibn Usayd, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to say in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Prophet, then Abu Bakr, then Umar. And Ali ibn Abi Talib was given three traits; for one of them to be mine would be dearer to me than red camels: he married Fatimah and she bore him children, he closed the doors except his door, and he gave him the banner on the day of Khaybar."
"5603","Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn al-Majishun Yusuf narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was such that we would compare no one to him, then we would say: The best of people is Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Uthman, then we would make no preference."
"5604","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, similar to it."
"5605","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Layth ibn Sa'd, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Umar, similar to it. He said: So that would reach the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would not object to it."
"5606","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud in prayer as the writing-teacher teaches children."
"5607","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to me, Ayyub ibn Thabit al-Madani narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalid ibn Kaysan saying: I was sitting with Ibn Umar when a youth passed dragging his lower garment, so he said to me: Call him, call him. He said: So I called him. He said: So he said to him: Lift your izar. He said: So he lifted it above his ankles. Then Ibn Umar said: Such is the izar of the Messenger of Allah, or he said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to wear the izar."
"5608","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Kaysan, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days, and if he dies of it he will enter the Fire."
"5609","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Qudamah ibn Musa, from Ayyub ibn Husayn al-Tamimi, from Abu Alqamah the freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Yasar the freedman of Ibn Umar, he said: Ibn Umar saw me while I was praying after dawn had risen. He said: O Yasar, how many have you prayed? I said: I do not know. He said: You do not know! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while we were praying this prayer and said: Let your present inform your absent that there is no prayer after Fajr except two prostrations."
"5610","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Nukri narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, my father informed me, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah accepts the repentance of His servant as long as he has not reached the death-rattle."
"5611","Al-Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar: From where is it permissible for me to enter ihram for umrah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed it for the people of Madinah from Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Syria from al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd from Qarn."
"5612","Al-Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Zayd, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, when a man asked him about fruit, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its ripeness appears."
"5613","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Khaliq ibn Salamah informed us, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying at the minbar - and he gestured to the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about drinks, so he forbade them: gourds, hollowed stumps, and varnished jars. I said: O Abu Muhammad, and coated vessels? We thought he had forgotten it. He said: I did not hear it that day from Abd Allah ibn Umar, though he used to dislike it."
"5614","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Salim ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ali ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever leads a blind man forty steps, Paradise becomes due for him."
"5615","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from misappropriated spoils."
"5616","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"5617","Amr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"5618","Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak al-Hanafi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the House, and there will come one who will forbid you from that, while Ibn Abbas was sitting beside him."
"5619","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Thabit al-Taymi, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Night prayer is two by two, then if you fear - or dread - dawn, then one."
"5620","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Tawus, he said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid jar-nabidh and gourds? He said: Yes."
"5621","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Night prayer is two by two, then if you fear dawn, pray witr with one."
"5622","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"5623","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd and Mu'adh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"5624","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Labid, from Abu Salamah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Let not the Bedouins overcome you regarding the name of your prayer. Indeed it is Isha, while they call it darkness with camels."
"5625","Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to me, that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad saying: I was with Abd Allah ibn Umar when a man came to bid him farewell, so Ibn Umar said to him: Wait, I will bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bid us farewell: I entrust your religion to Allah, and your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds."
"5626","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are three, two should not converse privately excluding their companion, for that grieves him. He said: What if they are four? He said: It will not harm you."
"5627","Abu Bakr al-Ramadi narrated to me, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' - meaning Ibn Umar - narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go to relieve himself at al-Mughammas. Nafi' said: About two miles from Makkah."
"5628","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, saying: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who came for umrah, circumambulated the House but did not walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah - may he go to his wife? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and seven between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and indeed in the Messenger of Allah there is a good example for you."
"5629","Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Amr, Hammad said: And Layth, from Amr, from Ibn Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not persist in begging, for whoever extracts something from us thereby, no blessing will be in it for him."
"5630","Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and indeed in the Messenger of Allah there was a good example for you."
"5631","Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, that Ibn Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs, except the dog of livestock or the hunting dog. It was said to Ibn Umar: Abu Hurayrah says: Or the dog of crops? He said: Abu Hurayrah has crops."
"5632","Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim al-Hudhali narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ibn Umar, that he bought mangy camels from Sharik al-Nawwas and found something in them, so he said: We accept the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No infection without Allah's decree."
"5633","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Budayl ibn Warqa, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about an i'tikaf vowed upon him, so he ordered him to perform i'tikaf and fast. While he was in i'tikaf, the people shouted takbir, so he said: What is this, O Abd Allah? He said: The captives of Hawazin, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has freed them. So Umar said: And that slave-girl too - send her with them."
"5634","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Ibn Umar, that he said to a man who ate much: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. So the man said: As for me, I believe in Allah and His Messenger."
"5635","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Amr, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah: We asked him about a man who circumambulated the House but did not walk between al-Safa and al-Marwah in umrah - may he go to his wife? He said: No. And they asked Ibn Umar about it, so Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, circumambulated the House seven times, prayed two rak'ahs behind the Maqam, and walked between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and indeed in the Messenger of Allah there is a good example for you."
"5636","Ghassan narrated to us, from Thabit, from Asim, from Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq, from Abd Allah ibn Umar: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about night prayer - while I was between them. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two by two, then if you fear dawn, pray one rak'ah, and two rak'ahs before the morning prayer."
"5637","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to me, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Wednesday and Thursday, freedom from the Fire will be written for him."
"5638","Suwayd narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Bakr, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"5639","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the mosque of Quba, then some Ansar came greeting him while he was in prayer, and Suhayb was with him. So I asked him how he responded to them? He said: He would gesture to them."
"5640","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: Two men came from the east and gave sermons, and the people were amazed at their praise. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Some eloquence is magic, or: Among eloquence is magic."
"5641","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, that two men came in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and gave sermons, and the people were amazed at their speech. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: Among eloquence is magic, or: Some eloquence is magic."
"5642","Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that he informed him, that he used to see Ibn Umar with the button of his shirt undone, so he was asked about that? He said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it."
"5643","Abu Yusuf Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, that Abd Allah ibn Umar used to dye his beard yellow with khaluq. It was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, you dye your beard yellow with khaluq? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dyeing with it, and no dye was dearer to him than it, and he used to dye all his clothes with it, even his turban."
"5644","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque of Quba - the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Awf - praying in it, then some Ansari men came in and greeted him while he was in prayer. So I asked Suhayb - who had entered with him - how did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act when greeted? He said: He would gesture with his hand."
"5645","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: I visited Ibn Umar - my father had sent me to him - and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah will not look at one who drags his izar out of pride."
"5646","Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Ibn al-Darawardi narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that he used to dye with yellow. He was asked about that, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dye with it, for I saw him dyeing his clothes with it, even his turban."
"5647","Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu Hisham al-Ayli, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every land and sea animal that has no flowing blood has no slaughter requirement."
"5648","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him. And he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on his mount wherever it turned with him, and Ibn Umar recited: {So wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah}."
"5649","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I read to Fudayl, from Abu Hariz, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we used to count fasting Arafah as fasting a year."
"5650","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he prayed Maghrib with them at Jam' with one adhan and iqamah, then he said: The prayer! Then he prayed Isha. He was asked about that, so he said: Thus I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at this place."
"5651","Abu al-Harith Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned her to me until I divorced her while she was pure."
"5652","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, Sa'id ibn Jubayr heard saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the two who invoked mutual curses: Your reckoning is upon Allah; one of you is lying, there is no way for you to her. He said: O Messenger of Allah, my wealth! He said: You have no wealth. If you told the truth about her, it is for what you made lawful of her private part, and if you lied, that is further from you."
"5653","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Umar passed by youths of Quraysh who had set up a bird and were shooting at it, and they had assigned to the bird's owner every arrow of theirs that missed. When they saw Ibn Umar they dispersed. So Ibn Umar said: Who did this? May Allah curse whoever did this! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed whoever takes a living creature as a target."
"5654","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr and Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling habal al-habalah."
"5655","Suwayd narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Dawud, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I saw Ibn Umar when silver was due upon him, he would give its value in dinars when it had a price. And when dinars were due upon him, he would give silver at its value."
"5656","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: When you take one of them for the other, let no sale remain between you when you part. Yahya said: And by that we abide."
"5657","Mujahid ibn Musa al-Khuttalli narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, he said: I was asked about the two who invoke mutual curses in the time of Mus'ab: Are they separated? I did not know what to say, so I went in the morning to the house of Abd Allah ibn Umar and asked permission. They said: He is sleeping, then he heard my voice and said: Ibn Jubayr? Permit him. He said: So I entered upon him, and he said: Nothing brought you at this hour except a need. He said: He was spread out on the saddle-cloth of his mount, pillowed on a cushion stuffed with fiber - or chaff. So I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, are the two who invoke mutual curses separated? He said: Glory be to Allah! Yes; the first to ask about this was so-and-so the son of so-and-so. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if one of us saw his wife committing indecency, what should he do? If he speaks, he speaks of a grave matter, and if he is silent, he is silent over the like of that? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer him. Later, he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, what I asked you about has befallen me. So Allah sent down the verses in Surat al-Nur: {And those who accuse their wives} to the end of the verse. He said: So he called the man and recited them to him, admonished him, reminded him, and informed him that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. He said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I did not lie against her. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the woman and recited them to her, admonished her, reminded her, and informed her that the punishment of this world is lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. She said: By Him who sent you with the truth, he did not tell the truth, indeed he lied. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began with the man, and he testified four testimonies by Allah that he was of the truthful, and the fifth that the curse of Allah be upon him if he was of the liars. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called the woman, and she testified four testimonies by Allah that he was of the liars, and the fifth that the wrath of Allah be upon her if he was of the truthful. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated them."
"5658","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Husayn, meaning Ibn Qays al-Rahabi, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw as if in his hands were two bracelets of gold. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So I blew them and they flew away, and they are the two liars of my nation: the master of Yamamah and the master of Yemen, and they will not harm my nation at all."
"5659","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Husayn, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not proper for a man to burden his slave with the heat and cold of his food; when he is present, he should set him aside from it."
"5660","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Malik, from Ata, he said: Ibn Umar said: A time came upon us when none of us saw himself more entitled to dinars and dirhams than his Muslim brother, until later here, when dinars and dirhams became dearer to one of us than his Muslim brother. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When people are miserly with dirhams and dinars, trade with inah, follow the tails of cows, and abandon jihad, Allah will send humiliation upon them, then He will not remove it from them until they return to their religion."
"5661","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey of his. When prayer time came, the people alighted, and a shepherd saw them, so he alighted striking the ground with his hand and performed tayammum, then called the adhan. He said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the fitrah. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. He said: He has come out of the Fire."
"5662","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, Ata ibn Abi Riyah narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not wake at any hour of the night except that he ran the siwak over his mouth."
"5663","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Abu Hayyan al-Taymi narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Umar, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a Bedouin came to him and said: Will you accept something good? Testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. He said: And who will testify for you? He said: This salam tree. So he called it while it was on the bank of the valley, and it came plowing the earth until it stood before him. So he asked it to testify and it testified three times, then it returned to its place. So the Bedouin said: I will go to my people; if they follow me I will bring them to you, otherwise I will return to you and be with you."
"5664","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Layth, from Ata, Tawus, and Mujahid, from Jabir, Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not circumambulate - he and his companions for their umrah and hajj - except one tawaf."
"5665","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on a donkey while facing Khaybar."
"5666","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah informed me, that Sa'id ibn Yasar Abu al-Hubab informed him that he heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying while facing Tabuk."
"5667","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Amr ibn Yahya, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on a donkey while facing Khaybar."
"5668","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abu Bakr, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr on the camel."
"5669","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz - meaning al-Qasmali - narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, he said: Ibn Umar heard a man saying: By my father. So Ibn Umar said: Do not swear by it; Umar used to swear by it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not swear by it."
"5670","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hazm narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Burdah, he said: I came to Madinah, then Abd Allah ibn Umar came to me and said: Do you know why I came to you? He said: I said: No. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever loves to maintain ties with his father in his grave, let him maintain ties with his father's brothers after him. There was brotherhood and affection between my father Umar and your father, so I loved to maintain that."
"5671","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Umar, that he used to raise his hands whenever he bowed and whenever he rose. I said: What is this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood in the two rak'ahs, would say takbir and raise his hands."
"5672","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gourds and varnished jars. He said: And I think he said: And hollowed stumps."
"5673","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Furat narrated to us, he said: Two men disputed before Muharib, so a man testified against one of them. The one testified against said: By Allah, I know him to be a truthful man, and if asked about him he would be praised - or commended - yet he testified against me falsely; I do not know what drove him to that? He said: So Muharib ibn Dithar said: O man, fear Allah! I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The false witness's feet will not move until Hell becomes due for him, and the birds on the Day of Resurrection will beat with their wings and cast out what is in their bellies, having no claim. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was admonishing a man."
"5674","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Umar, he said: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and it was a dark night - or a rainy night - the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Pray in your dwellings."
"5675","Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to me, that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad saying: I was with Abd Allah ibn Umar when a man came to bid him farewell. So Ibn Umar said: Wait, I will bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bid us farewell: I entrust your religion to Allah, and your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds."
"5676","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the steps of the Ka'bah on the day of the Conquest and said: Praise be to Allah who fulfilled His promise, aided His servant, and defeated the Confederates alone. Indeed the killing of quasi-intentional killing with the whip and stick entails one hundred camels in blood-money, forty of them pregnant with their young in their bellies. Indeed every blood and pre-Islamic boast is under these two feet of mine, except the custodianship of the House and the watering of pilgrims, for I confirm them for their people as they were."
"5677","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar, when he went to his bed, would say: O Allah, You created my soul, and You take it; to You belong its life and death. O Allah, if You take it, forgive it, and if You keep it alive, protect it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being. A man of his children said to him: O father, did Umar say this? He said: One better than Umar used to say it. He said: So we thought it was from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5678","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Simak, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No prayer is accepted without purification, and no charity from misappropriated spoils."
"5679","Ahmad ibn Janab narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change gray hair and do not imitate the Jews."
"5680","Al-Hakam ibn Musa al-Simsar narrated to us, Hiql narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Urwah, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we enter upon the ruler who judges with a judgment we see as unjust, and we say: May Allah grant you success, and we look at a man among us and praise him?! He said: As for we, the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to count this as hypocrisy, so I do not know what you count it as?"
"5681","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over the well of Badr and said: Have you found what your Lord promised you true? Then he said: They hear what I say. That was mentioned to Aishah, so she said: He erred - meaning Ibn Umar - he only said: Now they know that what I used to say to them is the truth. Then she recited this verse: {Indeed you do not make the dead hear} until she finished the verse."
"5682","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The dead is punished by his family's weeping over him. I mentioned that to Aishah, so she said: He erred - meaning Ibn Umar - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only passed by a grave and said: The owner of this grave is being punished while his family weep over him. Then she recited this verse: {And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another}."
"5683","Zuhayr narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man called to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which part of the night is most responsive in supplication? He said: The last middle of the night."
"5684","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the edge of the sun appears, delay prayer until it rises. And when the edge of the sun disappears, delay prayer until it sets."
"5685","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not aim your prayer at sunrise, for it rises with the two horns of Satan."
"5686","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Ibn Umar, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me a word, briefly, that I may understand it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not get angry. I repeated twice, each time the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied to me: Do not get angry."
"5687","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will turn to him. If he returns, his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will turn to him. If he returns, his prayer will not be accepted for forty mornings. If he repents, Allah will turn to him. If he returns a fourth time, it will not be accepted for forty mornings, and if he repents, Allah will not turn to him, and He will give him to drink from the river of khabal. It was said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is the river of khabal? He said: A river of the pus of the people of Hell."
"5688","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, that Ibn Umar used to crowd at the two corners. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I saw you crowding at the two corners with a crowding I never saw anyone of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crowding with? He said: If I do so, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wiping them is expiation for sins. And I heard him saying: Whoever circumambulates the House a week and counts it, it will be for him like freeing a slave. And I heard him saying: He does not place a foot nor raise another except that Allah removes a sin from him thereby, writes a good deed for him thereby, and raises a degree for him thereby."
"5689","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr, that he heard his father saying: I said to Ibn Umar: Why do I see you touching only these two corners: the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner? He said: Ibn Umar said: If I do so, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Touching them removes sins. And I heard him saying: Whoever completes seven circuits and prays two rak'ahs, it will be like freeing a slave. And I heard him saying: No man raises a foot nor puts it down except that ten good deeds are written for him, ten evil deeds are removed from him, and ten degrees are raised for him."
"5690","And Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, he said: Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to me, that he heard his father saying to Ibn Umar: Why do I see you touching these two corners and no others? Meaning the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner. He said: If I do so, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Touching them removes sins, and no man raises a foot nor puts it down except that ten good deeds are written for him and ten evil deeds are removed from him. And I heard him saying: Whoever completes seven circuits and prays two rak'ahs, it is like freeing a slave."
"5691","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Did you do such and such? He said: No, by Him besides whom there is no god, I did not do it. So Jibril said to him: He did it, but Allah the Blessed and Exalted has forgiven him by his saying: There is no god but Allah. Hammad said: He did not hear this from Ibn Umar; between them is a man."
"5692","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about vessels? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade those vessels."
"5693","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, he said: I witnessed Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, when a man asked him about the talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he narrated to us from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he recited talbiyah, would say: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You, here I am. Indeed praise and blessing belong to You, and dominion; no partner have You. Ibn Umar said: And it was added: Here I am, here I am; here I am, and happiness; good is in Your hands; here I am, and desire and deed are to You."
"5694","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated, from Bakr, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Makkah reciting talbiyah for Hajj. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make it umrah, except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us will go to Mina while his organ drips with semen? He said: Yes. So the censers blazed at al-Batha, and Ali came from Yemen. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With what did you enter ihram, for your wife is with us? He said: I entered ihram with what the Messenger of Allah entered ihram with. Humayd said: So I informed the people of that, while Tawus was sitting, and he said: Thus is the hadith."
"5695","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha at al-Batha, then slept a sleep, then entered Makkah, and Ibn Umar used to do it."
"5696","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, Habib ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with both together. Bakr said: So I met Ibn Umar and informed him of Anas's saying. So Ibn Umar said: He only entered ihram for Hajj. So I returned to Anas and informed him of Ibn Umar's saying, and he said: You only count us as children - or as if we were children - Sa'id doubted."
"5697","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hunaydah, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah sends punishment upon a people, the punishment strikes whoever is among them, then they will be resurrected according to their intentions."
"5698","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Bashshar ibn Kidam, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Swearing is expiation or regret."
"5699","Bishr ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah, from al-Muhajir al-Shami, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears a garment of fame, Allah will clothe him on the Day of Resurrection with a garment of humiliation."
"5700","Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Bukayr the cousin of Hafs ibn Ghiyath al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Zayd al-Ta'i, Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a woman of Banu Ghifar, and when she came to him he saw whiteness on her flank, so he returned her and said: You have deceived me."
"5701","Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from A'idh ibn Nusayb, he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed inside the Ka'bah."
"5702","Wasil ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Layth, from Sa'id ibn Amir, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: In my nation there are over seventy callers, all calling to the Fire. If I wished I could inform you of their fathers and tribes. He said: Then we passed ponds, and we began to scoop with our mouths in them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not scoop, but wash your hands, then drink in them, for no vessel is better than the hand."
"5703","And with the same chain, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This tribe of Quraysh will remain safe until you turn them away from their religion as requital. He said: A man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, am I in Paradise or in Hell? He said: In Paradise. Then another stood to him and said: In Paradise or in Hell? He said: In Hell. Then he said: Keep silent from me as long as I am silent from you. Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have informed you of your dead among the people of Hell until you would distinguish them at death, and if I were ordered to do so I would do it."
"5704","And with the same chain, from Ibn Umar, that he said: Shall I show you the place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the Beast of the Earth will emerge? So he struck with his staff the crack in al-Safa and said: It has feathers and down, and a third of it will emerge in the time of a swift horse, three days and three nights. It will pass over them while they flee from it to the mosques, and it will say to them: Do you think the mosques will save you from me? So it will brand them, and they will be driven in the markets, and it will say: O disbeliever! O believer!"
"5705","Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you eat with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"5706","Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you eat with his left hand, for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"5707","Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Nu'aym al-A'raj, he said: A man asked Ibn Umar about mut'ah of women - while I was with him - so he became angry and said: We were not, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), fornicators nor adulterers. Then he said: By Allah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Before the Day of Resurrection there will be the Dajjal, the False Messiah, and thirty liars or more than that."
"5708","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Nu'aym al-A'raj, he said: A man came to Abd Allah ibn Umar - while I was with him - and asked him about mut'ah of women. So he became angry and said: By Allah, we were not, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), fornicators nor adulterers."
"5709","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Abu Raja al-Jazari, from Furat ibn Salman, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No household is patient for three days over hardship except that Allah brings them provision."
"5710","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Layth, from Umayr ibn Abi Umayr, from Ibn Umar, he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) breaking fast on Friday."
"5711","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, Abu Dihqanah narrated to us, he said: I was sitting with Ibn Umar. He said: A guest came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said to Bilal: Bring us food. So Bilal went and exchanged two sa' of dates for a sa' of better dates, while their dates were inferior. It pleased the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: From where is this? He informed him that he exchanged two sa' for a sa'. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return our dates to us."
"5712","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Abdi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, he said: My father narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Umayr al-Ansari, he said: I sat with Abd Allah ibn Umar and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. One of them said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Sweat will reach people on the Day of Resurrection. One of them meant: To his earlobe, and the other said: Until it bridles him. So Ibn Umar said: Like this. And Abu Asim described it, passing his finger from his earlobe to his mouth: This and that are the same."
"5713","Abu Ubaydah ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, Thuwayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Umar - raising the hadith - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is one who looks at his tents, servants, bliss, and couches over a journey of a thousand years, and the noblest of them to Allah is one who looks to Allah morning and evening. Then he recited this verse: {Faces that Day will be radiant, looking to their Lord}."
"5714","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of you loves his supplication to be answered and his distress to be removed, let him ease one in hardship."
"5715","Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clothed me with a silk suit of Sira' garments from what Fayruz gifted him. So I wore the izar and it overwhelmed me in width and length, so I dragged it, and I wore the rida and wrapped myself in it. Then he said: O Abd Allah, raise the izar; for whatever touches dust below the ankles is in the Fire. Abd Allah ibn Muhammad said: I never saw anyone rolling his izar more than Abd Allah ibn Umar."
"5716","Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, Aban ibn Abd Allah al-Bajali narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray before the Eid prayer nor after it."
"5717","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Sukayn narrated to us, Abd al-Mumin narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, dates for dates, like for like, measure for measure; whoever adds or seeks addition has engaged in usury."
"5718","Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah accepts the repentance of the servant so long as he has not reached the death-rattle."
"5719","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Umar: From where is it permissible for me to enter ihram for umrah? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed it for the people of Madinah from Dhu al-Hulayfah, for the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and for the people of Najd from Qarn."
"5720","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayr, he said: I heard a man ask Ibn Umar about selling fruit, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until its ripeness becomes apparent."
"5721","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of al-Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, from Layth, he said: Abu Muhammad narrated to me, he said: I watched Ibn Umar for a month and heard him in the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer reciting Say O disbelievers and Say He is Allah the One. He said: So I mentioned that to him, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a month, or twenty-five days, reciting in the two rak'ahs before the Fajr prayer Say O disbelievers and Say He is Allah the One, and he said: One of them equals a third of the Quran and the other equals a quarter of the Quran; Say He is Allah the One equals a third of the Quran, and Say O disbelievers equals a quarter of the Quran."
"5722","Dawud ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated to us, Salih ibn Umar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Dawud ibn Asim ibn Urwah ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi, he said: I asked Ibn Umar at Mina about the prayer here. He said: I prayed two rak'ahs with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and two rak'ahs with Abu Bakr, and two rak'ahs with Umar, and with Uthman for the early part of his caliphate two rak'ahs. When we prayed with them we prayed as they prayed, and when we prayed alone we prayed."
"5723","Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid ibn Bishr al-Sakuni narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Riyah ibn Abidah, from Usayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, nephew of Abd al-Majid, he being the son of Sawdah bint Abd al-Rahman, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: I wore a silk garment and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was by the chamber of Hafsah on a dark night, and he heard the rustling of the garment and said: Who is this? I said: Abd Allah ibn Umar. He said: Lift up your garment, for whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him. He said: And my lower garment that night was at the middle of my shins."
"5724","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy prophets have taken shade in the shade of a lote tree, neither extravagantly nor stripped bare nor worn out."
"5725","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Na'im, freedman of Umm Salamah, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar set out for Hajj until, when he was between Makkah and Madinah, he came to a tree he recognized and sat beneath it, then said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beneath this tree when a young man came from this mountain path until he stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have come to strive with you in the path of Allah, seeking thereby the Face of Allah and the Hereafter. He said: Are both your parents alive? He said: Yes. He said: Then return and be dutiful to them. He said: So he turned back and returned the way he had come."
"5726","Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us, from Harun ibn Antarh, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I broke the fast on a day in Ramadan. He said: Without excuse or travel? He said: Yes. He said: Evil is what you have done. He said: Yes indeed, so what do you command me? He said: Free a slave. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have never owned a slave. He said: Then fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot do that. He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I cannot even feed my family. He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing dates, and he said: Give this in charity to sixty poor persons. He said: To whom should I give it? He said: To the poorest you know. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava plains more needy than us. He said: Then give it in charity to your dependents."
"5727","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Sa'd, freedman of Talhah, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a hadith such that had I heard it only once or twice, until he counted seven times, and indeed I heard it more than that; he said: Al-Kifl of the Children of Israel would not refrain from any sin he did, then a woman came to him and he gave her sixty dinars on condition that he sleep with her. When he sat with her as a man sits with a woman, she trembled and wept, and he said: What makes you weep? Did I coerce you? She said: No, but this is a deed I have never done, and only need drove me to it. He said: Would you do this though you have never done it? He said: Then he got up and said: Go, and the dinars are yours. Then he said: By Allah, al-Kifl will never disobey Allah again. He said: Then he died that night, and in the morning it was written upon his door: Allah has forgiven al-Kifl."
"5728","Shayban narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Jamilah, from Abd Allah ibn Mawhab, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is a judge and judges unjustly will be among the people of Hell, and whoever is a judge and judges out of ignorance will be among the people of Hell, and whoever is a judge and judges justly, it is likely he will escape with neither reward nor punishment."
"5729","Khalifah ibn Khayyat narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Awn ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, he narrated to them, from Ibn Umar, he said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer, a man among the people said: Allah is Most Great, much greatness; much praise belongs to Allah; glory be to Allah morning and evening. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Which of you said those words? The people fell silent, then a man among the people said: I said them, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended nothing but good. So the Messenger of Allah said: The gates of heaven were opened for them. Ibn Umar said: I have not abandoned them since I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say them."
"5730","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abjar, from Thuwayr ibn Abi Fakhitah, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is one who looks over his kingdom for two thousand years, seeing its farthest extent, looking at his wives and couches; and the highest of them in rank is one who looks at the Face of Allah twice every day."
"5731","Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, who said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan wrote to Ibn Umar: Send up to me your need. He said: So Ibn Umar wrote: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you maintain. And I do not ask you for anything, nor do I refuse any provision Allah provides me through you."
"5732","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I read to Fudayl, from Abu Hariz, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: You and your wealth belong to your father."
"5733","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu al-Mundhir Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, that Ibn Umar saw some people and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable, when a man comes wanting to kill him, to be like the two sons of Adam: the killer in the Fire and the killed in Paradise."
"5734","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi informed me, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a jar of unripe-date drink while he was in the Mosque of al-Fadikh, and he drank it, and that is why it was called the Mosque of al-Fadikh."
"5735","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Said ibn Hassan, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to camp at Arafah in the valley of Namirah."
"5736","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Said ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Asim al-Thaqafi, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about prayer at Mina. He said: Have you heard of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes, and I believed in him. He said: He used to pray two rakahs at Mina."
"5737","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade joining dates together (eating two at once when sharing) until you ask permission of your companions."
"5738","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ibn Umar, that he kissed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5739","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Alqamah say: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave the beards and trim the moustaches."
"5740","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Yaqub, from Ibn Abi Num, that a man asked Ibn Umar about mosquito blood. He said: Where are you from? He said: From the people of Iraq. He said: Look at this one! He asks me about mosquito blood while they killed the son of the Messenger of Allah! And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: They (Hasan and Husayn) are my two sweet basils in this world."
"5741","Zuhayr narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muslim, freedman of Abd al-Qays, who said: A man said to Ibn Umar: What about witr, is it sunnah? He said: What sunnah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims prayed witr. He said: Is it sunnah? He said to him: Do you understand?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims prayed witr."
"5742","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said informed us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, that his uncle Wasi ibn Habban informed him, that he was standing praying in the mosque while Ibn Umar was facing him with his back resting against the qiblah of the mosque. When Wasi finished he left to his left toward Ibn Umar and sat with him. Ibn Umar said to him: What prevents you from leaving to your right? He said: Nothing, except that I saw you and came to you. Ibn Umar said: You have done well. Some people say: When you pray and finish, leave to your right. Ibn Umar said: When you pray and finish, leave if you wish to your right and if you wish to your left. And Ibn Umar said: And other people say: When one sits to relieve himself, let him not face the qiblah nor Bayt al-Maqdis. Yet one day I climbed upon our house and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieving himself, Abu Yala was unsure, facing Bayt al-Maqdis."
"5743","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Sallam, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, that they both bore witness that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while upon the minbar, said: People shall stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or Allah shall seal their hearts, and they shall be among the heedless."
"5744","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in the first rakah of the noon prayer, and his Companions thought he had recited Tanzil, the Surah of Prostration. He said: And I did not hear it from Abu Mijlaz."
"5745","Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not strike slaves, for you do not know what you may coincide with."
"5746","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abu Alqamah, freedman of Banu Hashim, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that he saw a freedman of his called Yasar praying after Fajr and forbade him. He said: It is only the remainder of my portion (of night prayer). Abdullah said to him: Why did you not delay it until daytime? Then Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while people were praying after the break of dawn, and said: There is no prayer after Fajr except two rakahs."
"5747","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asbagh ibn Zayd al-Juhani informed us, Abu Bishr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hoards food for forty nights has disassociated from Allah and Allah has disassociated from him, and any people of a courtyard among whom a man wakes hungry, the protection of Allah is removed from them."
"5748","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Nuhayk ibn Yarim, from Mughith ibn Sumayy, who said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr led us in prayer in the darkness before dawn, with Ibn Umar beside me. When he gave salam, I said: What prayer is this, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: This was our prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr and Umar. When Umar was killed, Uthman prayed it later in brighter light."
"5749","Abu Abdullah al-Nukri narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: My grandfather Abu al-Muthanna narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed four rakahs before Asr."
"5750","Abu Abdullah ibn al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: My grandfather narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep except with the siwak beside him; when he woke he began with the siwak."
"5751","Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musab ibn Sad, who said: Ibn Umar visited Abdullah ibn Amir while he was ill, and he said: What prevents you from supplicating for me? He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not accept prayer without purification."
"5752","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Safwan ibn Muhriz, that a man asked Ibn Umar: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the private conversation (Najwa)? He said: He used to say: The servant draws near to his Lord, and He places His covering over him and makes him acknowledge, saying: You did such-and-such, and you did such-and-such. He says: Yes, my Lord. He says: I concealed it for you in the world, and today I forgive it for you. He said: So he is given his record of good deeds, and he says: Here, read my record. And as for the hypocrites, they will be called out: These are those who lied against their Lord; indeed the curse of Allah is upon the wrongdoers."
"5753","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sad al-Ashhali al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to me, from Nuaym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the solitary by twenty-seven degrees."
"5754","Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ismah narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that among Thaqif there is a destroyer (tyrant shedding blood) and a liar."
"5755","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Muwaqqari narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Abu Hirm, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) encouraged jihad one day, and they gathered around him until they crowded him. In the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a palm stalk whose thorns had been stripped except one thorn he had not noticed. He said: Move back from me, like this, for you have crowded me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a mans belly and made it bleed. The man left saying: This is the deed of your Prophet, so what about (ordinary) people? Umar heard him and said: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if he struck you, he will give you your right from himself, and if you lied, I shall drag you by your turban until you soil yourself. The man said: Go in peace; I do not want to go with you. He said: I shall not leave you. Umar took him until he brought him to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This one claims you struck him and made his belly bleed; what do you think? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is it true I struck him? The man said: Yes, O Prophet of Allah. He said: Did anyone see that? He said: There were some Muslims here. He said: O Allah, I call upon the testimony of any man who saw that to inform me. Some Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, you made him bleed but did not intend it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take wealth for my striking you and go. The man said: No. He said: Then grant it to me (forgive it). He said: I shall not. He said: Then what do you want? He said: I want to retaliate against you, O Prophet of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. The man said to him: Come out from among these people. So he came out from among them and allowed the man the stalk to retaliate. He uncovered his belly, and Umar came to hold the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from behind, and he said: Spare us; you stumbled with your sandal and your teeth broke. When the man drew near to strike the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he threw the stalk, kissed his navel, and said: O Prophet of Allah, this is what I wanted, so that we may suppress the tyrants after you. Umar said: Your deed is more reliable than mine."
"5756","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you place your dead in the grave, say: In the name of Allah and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."
"5757","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: I asked Ibn Abbas about witr, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: One rakah at the end of the night."
"5758","He said: And I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: One rakah at the end of the night."
"5759","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Husayn narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, who said: Ibn Umar narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say when he settled in his bed: Praise be to Allah who sufficed me, sheltered me, fed me and gave me drink, who bestowed upon me and favored, who gave me and granted abundantly. Praise be to Allah in every circumstance; praise be to Allah, Lord of everything, Sovereign of everything, God of everything, and to You belongs everything; I seek refuge in You from the Fire."
"5760","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Abd al-Jabbar al-Ayli narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Sumayyah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a woman who sees in a dream what a man sees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: When a woman sees that and has a discharge, let her perform ghusl."
"5761","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani narrated to me, from Abbas al-Hajari, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My servant misbehaves and wrongs; shall I strike him? He said: Pardon him seventy times each day."
"5762","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf upon his mount on the day of the conquest of Makkah, touching the corners with a curved staff he had with him."
"5763","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Zimmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Harithi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath then sees something else better than it, its expiation is to abandon it."
"5764","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my ummah to my ummah is Abu Bakr, the firmest of them in Islam is Umar, the most truthful of them in modesty is Uthman ibn Affan, the best judge among them is Ali ibn Abi Talib, the most knowledgeable of them in inheritance law is Zayd ibn Thabit, the most knowledgeable of them in the lawful and unlawful is Muadh ibn Jabal, the best reciter among them is Ubayy ibn Kab, and every ummah has a trustee, and the trustee of this ummah is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"5765","Zuhayr narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Yahya informed me, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from his uncle Wasi ibn Habban, that he asked Abdullah ibn Umar about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: (He said) Allah is Greatest whenever he raised and whenever he lowered, then he would say: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, to his right; peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, to his left."
"5766","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, that they both said: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say upon the wood of his minbar: People shall stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or Allah shall seal their hearts, then they shall be among the heedless."
"5767","Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Aban ibn Yazid al-Attar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd Abu Sallam, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Ismail ibn Ibrahim."
"5768","Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from him, and I asked him, meaning Muslim, and Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to me, that he heard Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, and he also said: Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Maawi narrated to me, who said: I prayed beside Ibn Umar and began turning over pebbles. He said: Do not turn over pebbles, for turning pebbles is from Satan, and do as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, how did you see him do? He said: Like this, and he placed his left hand upon his left thigh and his right hand upon his right thigh, and pointed with the one next to the thumb. Muslim said: It reached us that it is the whip of Satan, and that a person is not attended (by Satan) while saying it with his hand like this."
"5769","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two, pray witr with one rakah, and pray two rakahs before the dawn prayer."
"5770","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, I said: The two rakahs before dawn, shall I prolong recitation in them? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two and pray witr with one rakah. I said: It is not about this that I ask you. He said: You are bulky! Will you not let me recite the hadith to you in full? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night two by two, pray witr with one rakah, then pray two rakahs before dawn as though the adhan were in his ears."
"5771","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ayyub and Budayl narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How is the night prayer? He said: Two by two; when you fear dawn, pray one rakah and make the last of your prayer witr. Then he asked him at the turn of the year, while I was in that place near the Messenger of Allah, and I do not know whether he was that man or another man, and he said to him the same."
"5772","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam and Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he prayed them (Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah) with one iqamah, and said: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did in this place."
"5773","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked mutual cursing (lian) between a woman and her husband and separated them."
"5774","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr, from Abu al-Abbas the blind poet, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besieged the people of Taif but gained nothing from them. He said: We are returning, if Allah wills. His Companions said: Shall we return without conquering? The Messenger of Allah said to them: Go forth to battle in the morning. They went forth in the morning and were wounded. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: We are returning tomorrow. That pleased them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed."
"5775","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Said ibn Ziyad al-Shaybani informed us, Ziyad ibn Subayh al-Hanafi narrated to us, who said: I was standing praying toward the House (Kabah) with an old man beside me. I prolonged the prayer and placed my hands upon my waist. The old man struck my chest with his hand unsparingly. I said to myself: What bothered him about me? I hastened to finish, and there was a boy sitting behind him. I said: Who is this old man? He said: This is Abdullah ibn Umar. I sat until he finished, and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what bothered you about me? He said: Is it you? I said: Yes. He said: That is standing stiffly in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid it."
"5776","Zuhayr narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus narrate from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hunaydah, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends to create a person, the angel of the wombs says turning aside: My Lord, male or female? And He says: So Allah decrees His command. Then he says: My Lord, wretched or blessed? So Allah decrees His command. Then he writes between his eyes what he shall meet, even the stumble he shall suffer."
"5777","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad, from al-Mughirah ibn Salman, from Ibn Umar, who said: I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten rakahs: two rakahs before the Fajr prayer, two before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, two after Maghrib, and two after Isha."
"5778","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, who said: Ibn Umar used to perform wudu three times each, attributing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ibn Abbas used to perform wudu once each, attributing it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5779","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Isa ibn Hafs narrated to us, my father informed me, that he was with Ibn Umar on the road to Makkah, and he led them in prayer, then returned to his mount and we returned with him. He turned and saw people praying, and said: What are these doing? I said: They are performing voluntary prayers. He said: Had I been one to pray voluntary (travel) prayers I would have completed my prayer. O son of my brother, I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he did not exceed two rakahs in travel until Allah took him, then I accompanied Abu Bakr and he did not exceed two, then I accompanied Umar and he did not exceed two, then I accompanied Uthman and he did not exceed two until Allah took him. And Allah said: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example."
"5780","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Said ibn Amir, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and passed a pool of water, and they lapped from it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lap, but wash your hands and drink, for there is no vessel cleaner than the hand."
"5781","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Dawud ibn Abi Asim, who said: I said to Abdullah ibn Umar while at Mina: How many rakahs do you pray here? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed two, Abu Bakr prayed two, Umar prayed two, and Uthman prayed it two for six years, then they prayed it four. When we prayed with them we prayed four, and when we prayed alone we prayed two."
"5782","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: Ibn Umar said: We were in an army the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent; the people scattered in flight and we fled. We were a group and said: We shall flee in the land and not come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), out of shame for what we did. Then some of us said: If we came to Madinah, bought provisions there and equipped ourselves. When we entered Madinah we said: If we presented ourselves to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: We waited for him at the Fajr prayer. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out we said: O Messenger of Allah, we are the deserters. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather you are those who return to battle; I am the refuge of the Muslims."
"5783","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Firas, from Abu Salih, from Zadham, that Ibn Umar slapped a slave boy of his then freed him, and said: I have nothing of its reward, this, and he took something from the ground. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever strikes his slave unjustly, he has no expiation but freeing him."
"5784","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Najrani, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drunkard, and he imposed the hadd upon him, then said: What is your drink? He said: Raisins and dates. He said: Do you mix them? Each one has reached (fermented) from the other."
"5785","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive and his Companions were numerous, we used to count Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, then fall silent."
"5786","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, that he used to enter ihram when his mount stood straight with him, and enter ihram after prayer, and he used to say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"5787","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abu Bakr ibn Umar, from Said ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr upon the camel."
"5788","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among mosques, except the Sacred Mosque."
"5789","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Islam is built upon five: testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, hajj of the House, and fasting Ramadan."
"5790","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Qatan, that a freedwoman of Ibn Umar came to him to greet him before leaving Madinah, and said: I am going out to the countryside, for times have become hard upon us. Ibn Umar said: Sit, Lakai (you uncouth one); I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever endures its (Madinahs) hardship and severity, I shall be for him an intercessor, or a witness, on the Day of Resurrection."
"5791","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Qatan ibn Wahb, from Yuhannas, that a freedwoman of Ibn Umar came to him and said: Peace be upon you, O Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: What is your matter? She said: I intend to go out to the countryside, and mentioned prices. He said to her: Sit, Lakai; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: None endures its hardship and severity but I shall be for him an intercessor, or a witness, on the Day of Resurrection."
"5792","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, that he prayed Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah (Jam) with one iqamah, then said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it."
"5793","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Said informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Malik, who said: I prayed with Ibn Umar Maghrib and Isha at Muzdalifah; he prayed Maghrib three and Isha two with one iqamah. When he finished, a man said to him: What prayer is this, O Abu Abd al-Rahman? He said: I prayed it with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5794","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to me, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said while standing upon the minbar: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."
"5795","Musab ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to me, from Nafi, Abdullah ibn Dinar and Zayd ibn Aslam, all informing him, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah shall not look on the Day of Resurrection at one who drags his lower garment in arrogance."
"5796","Musab narrated to us, Malik informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar (exchange marriage without dowry)."
"5797","Musab and Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us; Musab said: narrated to me, and Suwayd said: Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade najsh (false bidding to inflate price)."
"5798","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells pollinated date-palms, its fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise."
"5799","And from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes full possession of it."
"5800","And from Ibn Umar: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until their ripeness appears; he forbade (harm to) both seller and buyer."
"5801","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"5802","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he said: In the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to buy food, and he would send to us one who ordered us to move it from the place where we bought it to another place before we sold it."
"5803","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall sell upon the sale of another."
"5804","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a share he owns in a slave, and he has wealth reaching the price of the slave, he shall be assessed its just value, give his partners their shares, and it (the slave) shall be freed upon him; otherwise, whatever is freed of him is freed."
"5805","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, he said: I read to Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn. Abdullah said: And it reached me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the people of Yemen enter ihram from Yalamlam."
"5806","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You. He said: Abdullah used to add to it: Here I am, here I am, here I am, at Your service, and good is in Your hands, and desire and deed are to You."
"5807","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What shall the muhrim wear? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He shall not wear the shirt, nor the turban, nor trousers, nor leather socks, except one who finds no sandals, let him wear leather socks and cut them below the ankles; and he shall not wear of clothes what saffron or wars (yellow dye) has touched."
"5808","Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: One who misses the Asr prayer, it is as though his family and wealth were taken from him."
"5809","Ali informed us, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A townsman shall not sell for a bedouin; and he said: Do not meet merchants on the way, none of you shall sell upon the sale of another, and none of you shall propose over the proposal of his brother until the first suitor leaves or permits him to propose."
"5810","Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a share he owns in a slave, and he has wealth equal to its price, he shall be assessed its just value; otherwise, whatever is freed of him is freed."
"5811","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man called to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was upon the minbar and said: O Messenger of Allah, how is the night prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thus, with his finger describing it, two by two; when you fear dawn, pray one rakah making your prayer odd."
"5812","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: A man said while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the minbar: O Messenger of Allah, what may the muhrim kill of animals? He said: The crow, the kite, and the vicious dog. Jarir said: And Ayyub said to me: I said to Nafi: And the snake? He said: About that no two differ."
"5813","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touch the (Black) Stone, and I never passed by it since I saw him except I touched it. Nafi said: Ibn Umar used to crowd for it; when they saw him they made room for him. One day I fell into the crowd of people; a man placed his elbow behind me, the man in front fell, I fell behind, and I thought I would not escape until they killed me, while he insisted on going forward."
"5814","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: A man said while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the minbar: What shall the muhrim wear? He said: He shall not wear the shirt, nor the turban, nor trousers, nor the hooded cloak, nor leather socks, except one who finds no sandals, then what is below the ankles; nor anything of clothes touched by wars or saffron."
"5815","Shayban narrated to us, Harb ibn Surayj al-Minqari narrated to us, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: We used to withhold seeking forgiveness for the people of major sins, until we heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, and He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. He said: I have stored my supplication as intercession for the people of major sins of my ummah. He said: So we withheld from much of what was in ourselves, then we spoke afterwards and hoped."
"5816","Shayban narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab saw Utarid al-Tamimi selling in the market a striped silk garment; he was a man who frequented kings and gained from them. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw Utarid selling in the market a striped silk garment; if only you bought it and wore it for the delegations of Arabs when they come to you, and I think he said: and wear it on Friday? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Silk is worn in this world only by one who has no share in the Hereafter. Later, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought striped silk garments; he sent to Umar a garment, sent to Usamah a garment, and gave Ali a garment, saying: Tear it into headscarves among your women. Umar came with his garment and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me this though yesterday you said about Utarids garment what you said? He said: I did not send it to you to wear, but I sent it to you to benefit from it. As for Usamah, he went out in his garment, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at him with a look by which he knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disapproved of what he did. He said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you look at me, when you sent it to me? He said: I did not send it to you to wear, but I sent it to you to tear into headscarves among your women."
"5817","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, who said: The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You."
"5818","Muhammad ibn Bakkar Abu Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"5819","Abu Said Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Yala al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Nafi, freedman of Abdullah ibn Umar, informed me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray the two rakahs after Maghrib with his family, and the two rakahs after Isha with his family."
"5820","Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmawayh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Said al-Madini Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman in ihram shall not wear the face veil."
"5821","Muhriz ibn Awn Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. Malik said: Shighar is that a man marry his daughter on condition the other marry him his daughter."
"5822","Abu Amir al-Adawi, meaning Hawtharah ibn Ashras, narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Abi al-Sahba informed me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba (pumpkin vessels) and muqayyar (pitch-coated vessels for nabidh)."
"5823","Suwayd narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of the unborn fetus in the womb of a she-camel (habal al-habalah). He said: The people of Jahiliyyah used to trade in it; a man would buy a camel to be delivered when the she-camel gave birth, then the one in its belly gave birth."
"5824","And from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders each have the option against the other so long as they have not parted, except the sale with stipulated option. Malik said: And for this there is with us no known limit nor an acted-upon ruling concerning it."
"5825","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Yala narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is not one-eyed; the False Messiah, the Dajjal, is one-eyed, his right eye as though a protruding grape."
"5826","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Juwayriyah ibn Asma ibn Ubayd ibn Mukhariq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who misses the Asr prayer, it is as though his family and wealth were taken from him."
"5827","Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who drags his garment in arrogance, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5828","Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, that Abdullah ibn Umar informed him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment to Najd among whom was Abdullah; they gained much booty, and their shares were twelve camels each, and each man among them was given extra."
"5829","Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"5830","Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim man who has something to bequeath has the right to spend more than two nights except with his will written with him."
"5831","Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid us, when there were three people, that two of them whisper apart from the third."
"5832","And from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dies, his seat is shown to him morning and evening; if he is of the people of Paradise, then of the people of Paradise, and if he is of the people of Fire, then of the people of Fire, until Allah resurrects him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5833","Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed each of you is a shepherd, and each is responsible for his flock. The ruler over people is a shepherd over them and responsible for them; a man is a shepherd over his household and responsible for them; a mans wife is a shepherdess over her husbands house and his children and responsible for them; a mans slave is a shepherd over his masters wealth and responsible for it. Indeed each of you is a shepherd and each is responsible."
"5834","And from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard Umar swearing by his father while in a caravan traveling with them, and called to them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers; whoever swears, let him swear by Allah or be silent."
"5835","And from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off (the hand of) a thief for a shield worth three dirhams."
"5836","And from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give Zakat al-Fitr a sa of dates or a sa of barley; and Abdullah used to say: People made its equivalent two mudds of wheat."
"5837","And from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a ring of gold, placing its stone toward the inside of his palm when he wore it on his right hand. People made rings of gold. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the minbar, removed it and said: I used to wear this ring with its stone inside my palm. He threw it and said: By Allah, I shall never wear it again. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) discarded the ring, and the people discarded their rings."
"5838","And from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward each day. It was said to him: Abu Hurayrah says: Or a farm dog? He said: Abu Hurayrah is a farmer."
"5839","Abdullah narrated to us, Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he burned the date-palms of Banu al-Nadir; and concerning it Hassan says: chiefs."
"5840","And from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your term among the terms of the nations before you is like what is between Asr and sunset. Your parable and that of the Jews and Christians is like a man who hired workers and said: Who will work for me until midday for a qirat? The Jews worked until midday for a qirat. Then he said: Who will work for me from midday until Asr for a qirat each? The Christians worked. Then he said: Who will work from Asr prayer until sunset for two qirats each? Indeed you are those who work from Asr prayer until sunset for two qirats each; indeed you have double reward. The Jews and Christians became angry and said: We worked more and were given less. He said: Did I wrong you anything of your right? They said: No. He said: It is My bounty; I give it to whom I will."
"5841","And from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced horses; he sent the trained horses from al-Hafya, its course ending at Thaniyyat al-Wada, and raced the untrained horses whose course was from Thaniyyat al-Wada to the mosque of Banu Zurayq. He said: And he informed me that Abdullah used to race with them."
"5842","And from Abdullah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab dedicated a horse in the path of Allah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted a man upon that horse. Umar found him selling it, and Umar said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The one you mounted upon the horse, I found him selling it; shall I buy it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Do not buy it, nor take back your charity."
"5843","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of Hajjaj al-Anmati, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a mouse that fell into ghee. He said: If it was solid, take it and what is around it; if it was melted, or liquid, it is not to be eaten."
"5844","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Hold to the black seed, for in it is healing from every disease except death."
"5845","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There shall come peoples, or there shall be peoples, who pray the prayer for you; if they complete it, it is for them and for you, and if they fall short, it is against them and for you."
"5846","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah fight the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as mosques!"
"5847","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The parable of the mujahid in the path of Allah, and Allah knows who strives in His path, is like the fasting one, the devout, humble, bowing, prostrating one."
"5848","Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, from Abu Hurayrah; and from the hadith of Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you say to your companion on Friday while the imam preaches: Be silent, you have engaged in idle talk."
"5849","Ahmad ibn Jamil al-Marwazi narrated to us, from Marwan ibn Muawiyah, from Yasin ibn Muadh al-Zayyat, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever accepts Islam with something in hand, it belongs to him."
"5850","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to me, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, that he said: Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah informed me, that Abu Hurayrah heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: An ant bit a prophet among the prophets, so he ordered the ant village burned. Allah revealed to him: Because an ant bit you, did you destroy a nation among nations that glorifies Allah?"
"5851","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5852","And from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The cupper and the one cupped break their fast."
"5853","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah shall grasp the earth on the Day of Resurrection and fold the heaven with His right hand, then say: I am the King; where are the kings?"
"5854","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: An ant bit a prophet among the prophets, so he ordered the ant village burned. Allah revealed to him: Was it for an ant biting you that you burned a nation among nations that glorifies Allah?!"
"5855","Al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi informed us, from Bakr ibn Wail, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you carry (a bier), delay (walk with measured pace), for the leg is bound and the hand is restrained."
"5856","Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, in marfu form, who said: In Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider travels a hundred years without crossing it; and recite if you wish: And extended shade."
"5857","Muhammad ibn Yazid, brother of Karkhawayh, narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Zamah narrated to us, from Budayl, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you shall say: My soul has become wicked; but let him say: My soul has become heavy."
"5858","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, brother of Hajjaj, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He gives him understanding in religion. And he said: I am only a distributor, and Allah gives."
"5859","Al-Hudhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Jummani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This ummah shall act for a while by the Book of Allah, then act for a while by the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, then act by opinion; when they act by opinion, they have gone astray and led astray."
"5860","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Said, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among mosques, except the Sacred Mosque."
"5861","Al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjadah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan ibn Abi Farwah, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a bier: he said takbir, then placed his right hand upon his left hand."
"5862","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz, and from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When you say to your companion: Be silent, while the imam preaches, you have engaged in idle talk."
"5863","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, Abu Salamah and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam after two rakahs. Dhu al-Shimalayn ibn Abd Amr ibn Nadlah, a man of Khuzah, ally of Banu Zuhrah, said to him: Has the prayer been shortened, or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah? He said: It was neither shortened nor did I forget. Dhu al-Shimalayn said: Some of that has happened, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to those who prayed with him and said: Has Dhu al-Yadayn told the truth? They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, completed the prayer, and did not prostrate the two prostrations made for forgetfulness in prayer when the people prompted him."
"5864","Ahmad narrated to us, Mubashshir narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: People recited with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a prayer in which he recited aloud. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he turned to them and said: Did anyone recite with me? They said: Yes. He said: I say, why is the Quran contended with me? Al-Zuhri said: People took heed thereby and would not recite in what he recited aloud."
"5865","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Habib, from Amr ibn Hirm, from Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: Abu Hurayrah used to say: I traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr and Umar; all of them prayed, from leaving Madinah until returning to it, two rakahs while traveling and while staying at Makkah."
"5866","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Zubayr, Jabir informed me, that Abu Hurayrah informed him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from sleep, let him pour over his hands three times before inserting them, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"5867","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters a horse between two horses hoping it shall be outrun, there is no good in it; and whoever enters a horse between two horses not hoping it shall be outrun, there is no harm in it."
"5868","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Raja al-Jazari, from Yazid ibn Sinan, or Burd, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Hurayrah, be pious and you shall be a worshipper; avoid the forbidden and you shall be an ascetic; be good to the neighbor beside you and you shall be a Muslim; love for people what you love for yourself and you shall be a believer."
"5869","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Muhammad, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes charge of judging, it is as though he were slaughtered without a knife."
"5870","Khalid ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Abu Abdullah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is tried with judging between Muslims, let him not judge while angry; let him equalize them in gaze, sitting and gesture, and not raise his voice over either disputant."
"5871","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, mentioning Madinah: There shall be conquests, and there shall be people who call their clans with longing, while Madinah is better for them had they known."
"5872","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who heard Said ibn al-Musayyib hear Abu Hurayrah say: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife gave birth to a black boy. He said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colors? He said: Red. He said: Is there among them a dusky one? He said: Indeed among them are dusky ones. He said: And whence is that? He said: Perhaps a strain drew it. He said: And this one, perhaps a strain drew him."
"5873","Kamil ibn Talhah narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Amr ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that some men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We are people who stay in the sand; major impurity befalls us, and among us are menstruating and postpartum women, and we do not find water for four or five months? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is the earth (tayammum)."
"5874","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When heat intensifies, cool (delay) the prayer, for intense heat is from the exhalation of Hell. And the Fire complained to its Lord and said: My Lord, parts of me consume parts; so He permitted it two breaths: a breath in winter and a breath in summer; it is the most intense heat you feel and the most intense cold you feel."
"5875","Amr al-Naqid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five are of the fitrah: circumcision, shaving the pubes, trimming the moustache, clipping nails, and plucking the armpits."
"5876","And with the same chain, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raised his head from the last rakah in the Fajr prayer, said: O Allah, save Al-Walid ibn Al-Walid, and Salamah ibn Hisham, and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, and the oppressed in Makkah. O Allah, tighten Your grip upon Mudar, and make it years upon them like the years of Yusuf. Then he fell down prostrate."
"5877","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the imam recites: {Not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray}, and the imam says amin, then say amin; for the angels say amin upon his supplication, and whoever's saying amin coincides with the angels' saying amin, his past sins are forgiven."
"5878","And from Abu Hurairah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except Al-Masjid Al-Haram."
"5879","And from Abu Hurairah, that a Bedouin urinated in the mosque, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, and a bucket of water - or a pail of water - was poured over his urine, and he said: You were only sent as facilitators, and you were not sent as those who make things difficult."
"5880","And from Abu Hurairah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Hour will not come until the son of Mary descends as a just judge and an equitable leader; he will kill the pig, break the cross, abolish the jizyah, and wealth will overflow until no one accepts it."
"5881","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Hour will not come until you fight a people whose sandals are of hair."
"5882","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no Fara and no Atirah in Islam."
"5883","And from Abu Hurairah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not undertake journeys except to three mosques: this mosque of mine, Al-Masjid Al-Haram, and Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa."
"5884","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When Khosrau perishes there will be no Khosrau after him, and when Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him; and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the cause of Allah."
"5885","And from Abu Hurairah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No Muslim loses three children and then enters the Fire, except to fulfil the oath."
"5886","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in a single garment? He said: Does every one of you find two garments? Then Abu Hurairah said to the man who asked him: Do you know Abu Hurairah? For he used to pray in a single garment while his clothes lay placed upon the clothes-rack."
"5887","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A town-dweller must not sell on behalf of a Bedouin."
"5888","And from Abu Hurairah, that Umar passed by Hassan while he was reciting poetry in the mosque, and he glanced at him, so he said: I used to recite in it, and in it was one better than you. Then he turned to Abu Hurairah and said: I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Respond on my behalf; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit? He said: O Allah, yes."
"5889","And from Abu Hurairah, that a man from Banu Fazarah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My wife has given birth to a black boy? He said: Do you have camels? He said: Yes. He said: What are their colours? He said: Red. He said: Is there any grey among them? He said: Yes, indeed among them are grey ones. He said: Then how did that come to them? He said: Perhaps a strain drew it out? He said: And this one too, perhaps a strain has drawn him out."
"5890","And with his chain, from Abu Hurairah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not practise najsh, and let none of you sell over his brother's sale, nor propose over his proposal, nor let a man outbid his brother, nor let a town-dweller sell for a Bedouin, and let not a woman ask for her sister's divorce so as to empty what is in her bowl and be married instead; for her provision is upon Allah."
"5891","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Muslim Az-Zuhri, Saeed ibn Al-Musayyib informed me, that Abu Hurairah used to say: A questioner asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May a man pray in a single garment? The Messenger of Allah said: And does every one of you have two garments?"
"5892","Mansur narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Saeed ibn Al-Musayyib, that a man would come to Abu Hurairah asking him for a fatwa about praying in a single garment, and he would say: Do you know Abu Hurairah? He would say: It is you. Then he would say: I pray in a single garment, though my garment lies placed upon the clothes-rack."
"5893","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Al-Hakam ibn Abdullah ibn Saad Al-Ayli, that he heard Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that she heard Abu Hurairah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is for three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity."
"5894","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman At-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Saeed ibn Al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast; the rich are invited and the poor are left out, and whoever does not answer the invitation has disobeyed Aba Al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5895","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Uyaynah ibn Hisn Al-Fazari came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him kissing Hasan and Husayn. He said: Do you kiss, O Messenger of Allah? Ten have been born to me and I have never kissed any of them. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"5896","Abd Al-Ala ibn Hammad An-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Mamar narrating, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever catches a rakah of the Asr prayer before the sun sets, and a rakah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises, has caught it."
"5897","Ibrahim ibn Saeed Al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu Al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurairah informed me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping, I saw in a vision two bangles of gold, and their matter concerned me. He said: While I was sleeping, it was revealed to me: Blow upon them, so I blew upon them and they flew away, and I interpreted them as two liars who will emerge; one of them was Al-Ansi, the man of Sanaa, and the other was Musaylimah."
"5898","Ibrahim ibn Ararah narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Amr ibn Ayyash, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is indeed punished by the weeping of the living."
"5899","Abu Bakr ibn Abi An-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Abu An-Nadr narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Saad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People whose hearts are like the hearts of birds will enter Paradise."
"5900","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala At-Taymi narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Saad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"5901","Mansur narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Saad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's debt remains attached to him when he dies, until it is paid off on his behalf."
"5902","Amr ibn Ad-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Numan informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that he informed him, from Saeed ibn Al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand; for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand."
"5903","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ziyad Ash-Shami informed us, from Az-Zuhri, from Saeed ibn Al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever assists in the killing of a Muslim with half a word will meet Allah on the day he meets Him with written upon his forehead: Despairing of Allah's mercy."
"5904","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Al-Awzai, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ruler - or he said: prophet - but he has two confidants: a confidant who enjoins good upon him and forbids him evil, and a confidant who spares him no corruption; so whoever is shielded from its evil has been shielded."
"5905","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, Abu Al-Mughirah Abd Al-Quddus ibn Al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Al-Awzai narrated to us, Az-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be after me caliphs who act upon what they know and do what they are commanded, and there will be after me caliphs who act upon what they do not know and do what they are not commanded; so whoever denounces them is absolved, and whoever withholds his hand is safe, but whoever is pleased and follows along!"
"5906","Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd Ar-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ath-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the judge judges and strives and is correct, he has two rewards, and when he judges and strives and errs, he has one reward."
"5907","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things are all a duty upon the Muslim: visiting the sick, attending funerals, and saying Yarhamukallah to the sneezer when he praises Allah."
"5908","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you cleans himself with stones, let him do so an odd number of times."
"5909","Shayban narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the slave steals, sell him even for an uqiyyah. And the uqiyyah is forty dirhams."
"5910","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you consider what he wishes for; for he does not know what will be written against him in his wish."
"5911","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the women who frequently visit graves."
"5912","Yaqub ibn Mahan narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam was only appointed to be followed, so when he says takbir, say takbir, and when he bows, bow, and when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: Our Lord, to You is praise; and if he prays standing, pray standing, and if he prays sitting, pray sitting all together."
"5913","Al-Harith ibn Surayj narrated to us, An-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews split into seventy-one sects, and the Christians split into seventy-one - or seventy-two - sects, and my nation will split into seventy-three sects."
"5914","Abd Al-Ala ibn Hammad An-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that Abu Hind cupped the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the crown of the head, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of the Ansar, marry to Abu Hind and marry from him. And he said: If there is good in anything with which you treat yourselves, it is cupping."
"5915","Mahmud ibn Khidash narrated to us, Abbad ibn Al-Awwam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tribulation continues to afflict the believing man and believing woman: in his body, his wealth, and his child, until he meets Allah with no sin upon him."
"5916","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Ar-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The days of Mina are days of eating and drinking."
"5917","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we find in ourselves things we would hate to speak of, though we would rather have all upon which the sun has risen. He said: Have you found that? They said: Yes. So he said: That is pure faith."
"5918","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not prevent Allah's female servants from Allah's mosques, but let them go out unattired."
"5919","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found the smell of garlic in the mosque, so he said: Whoever eats of this plant, let him not come near our mosque."
"5920","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning the fetus: a ghurrah, a male or female slave. He said: Then the one against whom judgment was passed said: Is blood-money paid for one who neither ate, nor drank, nor cried out and raised his voice? Such as that goes unavenged? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This one speaks the speech of a poet; in it is a ghurrah: a male slave or a female slave."
"5921","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, from Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Black seed is a cure for every disease, except the Sam. They said: And what is the Sam? He said: Death."
"5922","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrated in {Sad}."
"5923","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human, and perhaps some of you may be more eloquent in presenting his case than others; so whomever I award something from his brother's wealth, I am only awarding him a piece of the Fire."
"5924","Abu Saeed Al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four rivers gushed forth from Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile - the Nile of Egypt - Sayhan, and Jayhan."
"5925","Abu Mamar Al-Hudhali narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: Amin, amin, amin. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when you ascended the pulpit you said: Amin, amin, amin? He said: Jibreel came to me and said: Whoever reaches the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven, then enters the Fire, may Allah distance him; say: Amin, so I said: Amin. And whoever reaches his parents - or one of them - and does not treat them kindly, then dies and enters the Fire, may Allah distance him; say: Amin, so I said: Amin. And at whom you are mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you, then dies and enters the Fire, may Allah distance him; say: Amin, so I said: Amin."
"5926","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Abd Ar-Rahim narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, we find in ourselves something we would hate to speak of, though we would rather have all upon which the sun has risen. So he said: Have you found that? They said: Yes. He said: That is pure faith."
"5927","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Quraysh ibn Anas narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best of you to my family after me. Abu Khaythamah said: People say: to his family, but this one said: to my family."
"5928","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday: on it Adam was created, on it he was admitted to Paradise, and on it he was sent down from it."
"5929","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most perfect of the believers in faith are the best of them in character, and the best of you are the best of you to their women."
"5930","Muhammad ibn Al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, with the like of it."
"5931","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: Move to Umm Sharik, and do not deprive us of yourself. Abu Khaythamah said: Meaning Fatimah bint Qays."
"5932","Bishr ibn Al-Walid Al-Kindi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Al-Ala Ar-Razi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call grapes karm; for karm is the heart of the believer."
"5933","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Saeed, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."
"5934","Abd Al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's anger intensified against a people who broke an egg upon the head of their prophet while he was calling them to Allah."
"5935","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: I am the son of noble chieftains. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble, son of the noble is Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim."
"5936","Abd Ar-Rahman ibn Salih Al-Azdi narrated to us, Abd Ar-Rahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent Allah's female servants from Allah's mosques, but let them go out unattired."
"5937","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Among the rights of a Muslim upon a Muslim are: attending the funeral, returning the greeting, visiting the sick, saying Yarhamukallah to the sneezer when he praises Allah, and accepting an invitation."
"5938","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat she tied up; she neither fed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth."
"5939","Abu Hisham Ar-Rifai narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, Al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Al-Agharr, from Abu Hurairah and Abu Saeed, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When half the night - or a third of the night - has passed, He commands a caller who calls: Is there any supplicant so he may be answered? Is there any asker so he may be given what he asks? Is there any seeker of forgiveness so I may forgive him? Is there any repentant one so he may be turned to?"
"5940","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Hafs narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it, and he added in it: Until dawn breaks."
"5941","Saeed ibn Yahya narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Fajr prayer and prayed it early in the darkness, then prayed it the next day and brightened it a little, then said: Where is the questioner about the prayer time? The time is between these two: yesterday's, and my prayer today."
"5942","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is one who wishes upon Allah, and He says: To you is that and the like of it with it; except that when it is said to him: To you is such and such, he says: Is all of that for me? He said: And the like of it with it."
"5943","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created Paradise and the Fire, He sent Jibreel to Paradise and said: Go and look at it and at what I have prepared for its people in it. He said: So he went and looked at it, then returned and said: By Your might, I feared that no one would enter it. Then He sent him to the Fire and said: Go and look at it and at what I have prepared for its people in it. He said: So he went, and there it was, mounting upon one another. He said: By Your might, no one who hears of it will enter it. He said: Then He commanded it, and it was surrounded by desires, then He said: Return and look at it and at what I have prepared for its people. He said: So he looked at it and said: By Your might, I feared that none would be saved except that he would enter it."
"5944","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am only a human, and perhaps some of you may be more eloquent in presenting his case than others; whoever I award something from his brother's wealth, I am only awarding him a piece of the Fire."
"5945","And from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman entered the Fire because of a cat she tied up; she neither fed it, nor gave it water, nor released it to eat from the vermin of the earth."
"5946","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None endures its hardship and strain but I will be an intercessor - or a witness - for him on the Day of Resurrection. And none leaves it out of dislike for it but Allah replaces it with what is better than him; and Madinah is better for them, if only they knew."
"5947","And from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade preparing nabidh in muzaffat, dubba, hantamah, and naqir. And he said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"5948","And from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until thirty lying impostors emerge, each of them lying against Allah and His Messenger."
"5949","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man remains young in love of two things: love of life, and love of wealth."
"5950","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him: the good deed is ten times its like up to seven hundredfold, except fasting, for it is Mine, and I reward for it; he leaves food and desire, and leaves drink for his desire for My sake; it is Mine, and I reward for it."
"5951","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves dependents, it is to me."
"5952","And from Abu Hurairah, that he used to lead them in prayer and say takbir each time he lowered his head and raised it, and when he finished, he said: I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5953","And from Abu Salamah, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah prostrating in: {When the sky splits open}, and when he finished, I said to him: You prostrated in a surah in which prostration is not performed? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in it."
"5954","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Satan confronted me in this prayer place of mine, so I seized him and strangled him, until I could feel the cold of his tongue upon the back of my hand; and were it not for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have remained tied up for you to look at."
"5955","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every beast of prey with fangs, and the mujaththamah, and the domestic donkey."
"5956","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah said: I am Ar-Rahman, and it is the womb; I derived for it a name from My Name, so whoever joins it I join him, and whoever severs it I sever him and cut him off."
"5957","And from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood upon Al-Hajun in the year of the Conquest and said: By Allah, you are the best of Allah's land, and had I not been expelled from you I would not have left; and it was not made lawful for anyone before me, and it was only made lawful for me for an hour of the day, then from this hour of mine it is forbidden; its trees are not to be cut, nor its grass to be uprooted, and nothing lost is to be picked up except by one announcing it. A man called Shah - and people claimed he was Al-Abbas - said: O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir, for it is for our houses and graves. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except idhkhir."
"5958","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women."
"5959","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that when An-Najashi died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed them that he had died, so seek forgiveness for him."
"5960","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurairah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so oppose them."
"5961","Abu Khaythamah and Al-Muqaddami narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, raising it, he said: Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer and confuses him, until he does not know how much he prayed; so whoever finds something of that, let him prostrate two prostrations while seated."
"5962","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has not permitted anything as He has permitted a prophet to chant the Quran."
"5963","And from Abu Hurairah, in narration: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven. And whoever stands the Night of Decree with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."
"5964","And from Abu Hurairah, in narration: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into his vessel until he has washed it three times; for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"5965","And from Abu Hurairah, in narration: Whoever catches a rakah of a prayer has caught it."
"5966","And from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is black seed; for in it is cure from every disease, except the Sam. And the Sam is death."
"5967","Muhammad ibn Ishaq Al-Musayyibi narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to me, from Yunus, from Az-Zuhri, that he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman informed me, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes upon one of you until he does not know how much he prayed; so when he does that, let him prostrate two prostrations while seated."
"5968","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd Ar-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be trials like the winds of summer; the one seated in them is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking; whoever reaches out for them, they will reach out for him."
"5969","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever catches a rakah of the prayer has caught the prayer."
"5970","Abu Saeed Al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris Al-Awdi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rakah of the prayer has caught it all."
"5971","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, that Saeed ibn Al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to him, that Abu Hurairah narrated to them, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced to them the death of An-Najashi on the day he died, and said: Seek forgiveness for your brother."
"5972","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to encourage standing in Ramadan without firm obligation."
"5973","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not practise najsh."
"5974","Al-Ashajj narrated to us, Ishaq, meaning Ar-Razi, narrated to us, Muawiyah narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no newborn born but Satan touches him, so he begins crying loudly from Satan's touching him, except Isa son of Maryam and his mother; for Allah says: {I seek refuge for her with You and her offspring from the accursed Satan}."
"5975","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the Night of Decree, so he said: I was shown it, then I was made to forget it, and perhaps that is better for them; but seek it in the last ten of Ramadan."
"5976","Abu Hammam narrated to us, Abd Ar-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr Al-Laythi, Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you rises from his sleep, let him pour from his vessel over his hands; for he does not know where his hand spent the night. So Qayn Al-Ashjai said: What if we come to this mihras of yours? He said: I seek refuge with Allah from your evil, O Qayn."
"5977","Sahl ibn Zanjalah Ar-Razi narrated to us, Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Qurrah narrated to me, he said: Az-Zuhri narrated to me, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to me, he said: Abu Hurairah narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the most beloved of My servants to Me are those quickest to break the fast."
"5978","Muhammad ibn Jami Al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd As-Salam ibn Abi Al-Janub narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited before Fajr, then he recited six rakahs, turning right and left in every two rakahs, so we thought that for every section there were two rakahs, and he did not say salam."
"5979","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will descend upon Khuz and Kirman among eighty thousand wearing hair shoes and wearing tayalisah, as though their faces were hammered shields."
"5980","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change grey hair, and do not resemble the Jews nor the Christians."
"5981","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The Jews split into seventy-one sects, and the Christians split into seventy-one - or seventy-two - sects. He said: One of the two groups: seventy-one, and the other: seventy-two; and my nation will split into seventy-three sects. Muhammad ibn Amr doubts."
"5982","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A funeral passed by him and they praised it with good among the traits of good, so he said: It is due. Then another passed by him and they praised it with evil among the traits of evil, so he said: It is due. Then he said: You are Allah's witnesses on earth."
"5983","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Ghifar, Aslam, Muzaynah, and whoever is of Juhaynah are better than the two allies: Ghatafan, Asad, Hawazin, Tamim; and those beneath them, for they are people of horses and wool."
"5984","And from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Ibrahim was circumcised at the age of eighty, and was circumcised with the qaddum."
"5985","Muhammad ibn Jami Al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Abd As-Salam ibn Abi Al-Janub narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of neighbourhood is forty houses thus, and thus, and thus: right and left, front and back."
"5986","Nuh ibn Hatim, a Baghdadi, narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: Uyaynah ibn Hisn entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him kissing Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn. Uyaynah said: Do you kiss them, O Messenger of Allah? And I have ten and never kissed any of them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy."
"5987","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Al-Had narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought one who had drunk, so he said: Beat him; so among us was one who beat with his garment, and among us was one who beat with his sandal. One of the people said: May Allah disgrace you! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say thus; do not help Satan against him."
"5988","Abd Al-Ghaffar ibn Abdullah ibn Az-Zubayr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying while the muadhdhin was giving the iqamah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Two prayers together?"
"5989","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: I picked a shoulder for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the pot of Al-Abbas, and he ate it and stood to pray without performing ablution."
"5990","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has intercourse with an animal, kill him and kill it with him. Abu Yala said: Then it reached me that he retracted it."
"5991","Khalid ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Mamar, Yunus, Malik, and Al-Awzai, from Az-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rakah of the prayer has caught it. Mamar said: Az-Zuhri said: So we view Friday as part of the prayer."
"5992","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heart of the old man remains young in love of two things: love of life, and love of wealth. Ibn Arafah said: And I am one of them."
"5993","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Abd Ar-Rahman ibn Muhammad Al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lifespans of my nation are between sixty and seventy, and the fewest of them are those who exceed that. Ibn Arafah said: And I am among the fewest."
"5994","Hannad ibn As-Sari narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever intends the people of Madinah with evil, Allah will melt him as salt melts in water."
"5995","Ahmad ibn Ibrahim Ad-Dawraqi narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ismail Al-Halabi narrated to us, from Al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah making this takbir which you see, so I said to him: O Abu Hurairah, what is this takbir? He said: It is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5996","And from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the caller calls, Satan turns away passing wind; then when he finishes, he comes forward; then when the iqamah is pronounced, he turns away; and when it finishes, he comes forward, until he comes between a man and himself, saying: Remember such and such which he had not remembered, until he does not know whether he prayed three or four; so if one of you does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him prostrate two prostrations while seated."
"5997","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one early to Friday is like one offering a camel, and the one next is like one offering a sheep, and the one next is like one offering a bird."
"5998","And from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in the Isha prayer - after saying: Allah hears whoever praises Him - for a month in his qunut: O Allah, save Al-Walid ibn Al-Walid; O Allah, save Salamah ibn Hisham; O Allah, save Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah; O Allah, save the oppressed among the believers; O Allah, tighten Your grip upon Mudar; O Allah, make it years upon them like the years of Yusuf."
"5999","And from Abu Salamah, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah prostrating in {When the sky splits open}, so I said: O Abu Hurairah, I see you prostrating in {When the sky splits open}? He said: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in it, I would not have prostrated."
"6000","And from Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven. And whoever stands the Night of Decree with faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."
